Page 63 að: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|[aːð̠]}}
* {{rhymes|is|aːð|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|at||that}}. From {{inh|is|gem-pro|*þat|t=that}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|þæt}}, {{cog|got|𐌸𐌰𐍄𐌰}}.

====Conjunction====
{{head|is|conjunction}}

# [[that]]
#: {{ux|is|Hún sagði mér '''að''' þessi bók væri [[góður|góð]] [[lesning]].|She told me '''that''' this book was a good [[read]].}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|is|non|at||at, to}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*at||at, to}}. More at {{l|en|at}}.

====Particle====
{{head|is|particle}}

# [[to]] {{gloss|infinitive particle}}
#: {{ux|is|Mig [[langa]]r '''að''' lesa.|I want '''to''' read.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The infinitive particle '''að''' is the only infinitive marker in Icelandic.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|til að mynda}}

====Preposition====
{{head|is|preposition}}

# [[to]], [[towards]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{ux|is|[[ganga|Göngum]] '''að''' [[hús]]inu.|Let's walk '''towards''' the house.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der2|is
|að nafni
|ber er hver að baki, nema sér bróður eigi
|biðja að heilsa
|hlæja að
|fara að sofa
|að yfirlögðu ráði
|skara eld að sinni köku
}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|is|til}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Islex}}

-------- end text --------
