Page 292 af erlendu bergi brotinn: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
"Af X bergi brotinn" literally means "broken from an X rock". It is most likely a Biblically-inspired analogy describing each person as being carved out of a specific rock, with that rock therefore being their origin.

===Prepositional phrase===
{{head|is|prepositional phrase|head=[[af]] [[erlendur|erlendu]] [[berg|bergi]] [[brjóta|brotinn]]}}

# {{lb|is|higher register}} (a person who is) of a foreign origin or has a foreign background; (a person who) was born in a foreign country but now lives here

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|rekja rætur til|eiga rætur að rekja til}}
* {{l|is|útlendingur}}, {{l|is|erlendur}}, {{l|is|innflytjandi}}
-------- end text --------
