Page 437 Ak city: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|is|Ak-city|AK city}}

===Etymology===
A clipping of {{m|is|Akureyri}}, with the English word {{m|en|city}}.
Likely a humorous imitation of "Rvk city" (short for "[[Reykjavík]] City"), which has connotations of English-language tourism or metropolitanism.
Akureyri is however not a city but a town.
The term was first seen in print in 2014.

===Proper noun===
{{head|is|proper noun}}

# {{lb|is|humorous|informal}} [[Akureyri]] (town in the North of Iceland)

====Declension====
{{rfinfl|is|proper noun}}
-------- end text --------
