Page 681 andskoti: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
An [[Old Norse]] term meaning "opponent", from {{com|is|and-|skjóta|alt2=skoti|lit=he who shoots against you}}.

By extension, everybody's opponent is Satan. This meaning is attested in some old poems, including one claimed to be from 1180.<ref>[https://timarit.is/page/6483492#page/n139/mode/2up Að kenna kölska. Helgi Skúli Kjartansson. Són, 2009, p. 141.]</ref>

