Page 789 ari: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|ari}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*arô}}, from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*h₃érō}}. Proto-Germanic preserved a zero-grade ''-n''-suffix. This form is an Old Norse regularization as an ''an''-stem masculine noun. Compare the doublet {{m|is|örn}}, which was inherited from the same Proto-Germanic word, but regularized as a u-stem similarly to {{m|is|björn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈaːrɪ/}}
* {{rhymes|is|aːrɪ|s=2}}
* {{homophones|is|Ari}}

