===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈøyːkaˌstaːvʏr/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|aːvʏr}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|mathematics}} a numeral appearing in the [[fractional]] part of a [[number]] written in [[positional notation]] (i.e. after the [[radix point]]), e.g. a numeral in some [[decimal place]] in a [[decimal number]]

====Usage notes====
This word refers to the numerals themselves rather than their positions, so its meaning is not quite the same as that of English {{m|en|decimal place}} or {{m|en|place}}; however, it is often used in similar contexts, such as when counting decimal places, e.g. {{m|is||námunda að þremur aukastöfum|to round to three decimal places}}.

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|@s}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|hækka upp||to [[round up]], to change a number by removing decimals and incrementing the last decimal: 16.666 → 16.7}}
* {{l|is|jafna út||to raise or lower the value of a number by removing decimals}}
-------- end text --------
