#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1936|journal=Náttúrufræðingurinn|volume=6|issue=3|page=143|title=Um mýragróður Íslands|trans-title=On the moorland vegetation of Iceland|author=Steindór Steindórsson|passage=''Ýmsar aðrar starartegundir vaxa einnig í starungsmýrinni, svo sem blátoppastör, '''belgjastör''' og hárleggjastör, og sé mjög votlent, leita bæði gulstörin og fífan inn í ríki mýrastararinnar''.|translation=Other different sedge species also grow on the sedge moor, such as hoary sedge, '''grass-like sedge''' and hair-like sedge, and if it is very wet, both Lyngbye's sedge and cottongrass find their way into the black sedge's domain.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|date=25 January 1967|journal=Dagur|issue=6|title=Þættir af Flateyjardal|trans-title=Stories from Flateyjardalur|author=Helgi Hallgrímsson|page=5|passage=''Þar fann ég mikið af flóastör, hrafnastör, og '''belgjastör''', en í blautu halli fyrir ofan mýrina óx ígulstör.''|translation=There I found much bog sedge, rock sedge and '''grass-like sedge''', while on a wet slope above the moor grew star sedge.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1989|journal=Ráðunautafundur|volume=12|issue=1|page=153|title=Framræsla mýra|trans-title=Draining of a swamp|author=Borgþór Magnússon; Sturla Friðriksson|passage=''Veruleg auking varð einnig á þekju '''belgjastarar''' og blávinguls, en hann var eina grastegundin sem jók útbreiðslu sína að einhverju marki.''|translation=There was also a significant increase in the coverage of '''grass-like sedge''' and viviparous fescue, but this was the only grass species that increased its distribution to any degree.}}

