Page 1653 bévítans: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
A [[minced oath]], with {{m|is|bé||B}} being the first letter of {{m|is|bölva|bölvaður|cursed!}} and the latter half being derived from the (now uncommon) curse word {{m|is|ansvítans}}.

{{m|is|ansvítans|Ansvítans}} is an adjective derived from {{m|is|ansvíti}} (a [[contraction]] of {{m|is|andskoti||devil}} and {{m|is|helvíti||hell}}) that imitates the ending of {{m|is|andskotans}}.

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|-}}

# [[damned]], [[darned]] {{gloss|a mild curse word}}
#: {{uxi|is|'''Bévítans''' [[gigt]]in er að fara með mig.|That damn arthritis is just killing me right now.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|is|árans}}, {{l|is|ansans}}, {{l|is|déskotans}}
* {{seeSynonyms|is|andskotans}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|bévíti}}, {{l|is|bévítans}}, {{l|is|bévaður}}

