Page 1849 blátoppastör: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Carex.curta.jpg|thumb|''Blátoppastör'']]

===Etymology===
From {{af|is|blár|toppur|stör|t1=blue|t2=top; summit; crest|t3=sedge}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈplauː.tʰɔhpaˌstœːr/}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[hoary sedge]], [[white sedge]] ({{taxlink|Carex canescens|species}})
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1909|journal=Búnaðarrit|volume=23|issue=1|page=45|passage=''Þar til má telja hengistör (carex rariflora), gulstör (carex Lyngbyei), '''blátoppastör''' (carex canescens), hrafnastör (carex pulla) og hnappstör (carex capitata).''|translation=Looseflower sedge, Lyngbye's sedge, '''hoary sedge''', rock sedge and capitate sedge can also be considered.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1954|journal=Náttúrufræðingurinn|volume=24|issue=1|page=23|passage=''Bastarður þessi, sem er til orðinn við samæxlun tvibýlisstarar og '''blátoppastarar''', hefur ekki fyrr fundizt hér á landi.''|translation=This hybrid, which has emerged from the crossing of dioecious sedge and '''hoary sedge''', has not previously been found here in Iceland.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1978|journal=Tíminn|volume=62|issue=186|page=21|passage='''''Blátoppastör''' myndar blágræna toppa víða í mýrum, svo að auðvelt er að ná í hana o.fl. algengar starir og sef.''|translation='''Hoary sedge''' forms blue-green spikes far and wide in the swamp, so it is easy to get it and other common sedges and reeds.}}

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|f}}

{{C|is|Sedges}}
