Page 2081 bólakaf: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the synonymous phrase ''á bólandi kaf''. {{m|is|kaf|Kaf}} is to submerge, and {{m|is|bóla|bólandi}} presumably refers to air bubbles being visible on the surface, as in the figurative phrase {{m|is|bóla á|að bóla á einhverju|for something to be noticed}}.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[submerged]] under deep water; to dive deep; to become fully submerged
#: {{uxi|is|Bíllinn er á '''bólakafi'''.|The car is at the bottom of the lake.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Bíllinn fór á '''bólakaf'''.|The car went fully under water. / The car sunk to the bottom.}}
# {{lb|is|figurative}} to [[immerse]] oneself to the fullest with something; to be very occupied with something; to dive deep into a subject
#: {{syn|is|önnum kafinn}}
#: {{uxi|is|Hann sökkti sér á '''bólakaf''' í lærdóminn.|He immersed himself with his studies.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Hann er á '''bólakafi''' í vinnu.|He is buried in work.}}

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|n.sg.indef}}
-------- end text --------
