Page 2190 bresta: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈprɛsta/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ɛsta|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|bresta}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*brestaną}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*bʰres-||to burst, break, crack, split, separate}}.

Cognate with Faroese {{m|is|bresta}}, Swedish {{m|sv|brista}}, English {{m|en|burst}}, German {{m|de|bersten}}, Dutch {{m|nl|barsten}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-strong|brast|brustu|brostið}}

# to [[burst]], to [[break]]
#* Það er bara tímaspursmál hvenær stíflan '''brestur'''.
#*: ''It's only a question of time when the dam will '''burst'''.''
# {{lb|is|impersonal}} to [[cause]] to [[lack]] {{gl|to cause to experience a shortcoming of}} {{+obj|is|acc<someone><qq:preceding> + acc<something><qq:following>}} {{q|idiomatically translated as "lack" with the preceding accusative object as the subject}}
#: {{ux|is|Drottinn er minn hirðir, mig mun ekkert '''bresta'''.
|t=''The Lord is my shepherd, I shall not '''want''' (lit. “I shall want for nothing”)''.}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{is-conj-s3|br|e|st|mp=-}}

===Etymology 2===
Inflected form of {{m|is|brestur||crack, crackle}}.

====Noun====
