Page 2868 drýgja: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|drýgja}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*driugijaną}}, derived from {{m|gem-pro|*dreugaz||long-lasting}}, in the sense “eke out”. The sense “commit” may be carried over from the related strong verb {{m|gem-pro|*dreuganą}} (whence {{cog|ang|drēogan||to perform (a duty)}}, {{cog|got|𐌳𐍂𐌹𐌿𐌲𐌰𐌽||to perform military service}}), which was lost some time in the Old Norse period, but seems to be preserved in past tense {{m|non||draug}} on a Swedish runic fragment.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈtriːja/}}
* {{rhymes|is|iːja|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|drýgði|drýgt}}

# to [[commit]], to [[perpetrate]]
# to [[eke out]], to make something go further

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-w2|dr|ý|g|j=j}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to commit}} {{l|is|fremja}}

===References===
