|{{l|is|liggja á eggjum|t=to [[brood]], sit on eggs}}
|eggjasalad
|eggjaskurn
|páskaegg
}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|is|non|egg}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*agjō}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-|t=sharp, pointed}}.

Cognates include {{cog|ofs|egg}}, {{cog|osx|eggia}}, {{cog|nl|egge}}; {{cog|ang|ecg}} ({{cog|en|edge}}); {{cog|goh|egga}} ({{cog|de|Ecke}}); {{cog|sv|egg}}.

The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|la|aciēs|t=edge, sharpness}}, {{cog|grc|ἀκίς|t=point}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:edge}}

# {{lb|is|weapons}} the sharp [[edge]] of a [[knife]], [[sword]], or similar
#: {{syn|is|blað}}
# a sharp edge on a [[mountain]]

