Page 3198 eingetinn: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{compound|is|einn|t1=one|getinn|t2=begotten, conceived}}, past participle of {{m|is|geta||to conceive}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈein.cɛːtɪn/}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|-}}

# {{lb|is|now chiefly used in religious context}} [[only-begotten]] {{gloss|being the only child of one’s parent}}
# conceived in the womb without the physical input of a father; [[parthenogenic]]

====Usage notes====
The first sense is used in the Bible, creeds and other religious discourse, most often in reference to Jesus Christ. In this context, it is a translation of {{cog|grc|μονογενής}} and {{cog|la|ūnigenitus}}. The second sense, “parthenogenic”, is based on a misunderstanding of the word in reference to Jesus, taking it to refer to his [[virgin birth]] rather than his unique filial relationship to [[God the Father]], in essence understanding the {{m|is|einn|t=one}} in {{m|is||eingetinn}} to refer to the parent rather than the child.
-------- end text --------
