Page 3318 ekki baun: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|not a bean}}. The phrase is quite old; it is related to an older analogy of saying that something is less of a bellyful than a single bean, as a bean is quite small and insignificant.

{{m|is|ekki baun í bala|Ekki baun í bala}} is a more recent saying.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/(ˌ)ɛhcɪˈpøyːn/}}

===Adverb===
{{is-adv}}

# {{lb|is|colloquial}} [[not at all]], absolutely not, absolutely nothing
#: {{ux|is|Ég skil '''ekki baun'''.|I don't understand one [[iota]].|lit=I do'''n't''' understand '''a bean'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hann er '''ekki''' búinn að gera '''baun''' í allan dag.|He hasn't done anything at all today.|lit=He has'''n't''' done '''a bean''' all day.}}
#: {{ux|is|Það var '''ekki baun''' vont að fara í endajaxlatöku.|Getting my wisdom teeth out didn't hurt one bit.|lit=It was'''n't a bean''' bad to go to the wisdom tooth removal.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|is|alls ekki}}, {{l|is|alls ekkert}}, {{l|is|ekki neitt}}, {{l|is|ekkert}}, {{l|is|ekki baun í bala}}
