Page 3488 er: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ɛːr/}}
{{rfap|is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|er||is|pos=3rd person singular}}, analogical leveling of earlier {{m|non|es}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*isti}}, from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*h₁ésti}}.

Use with the 1st person singular is also by analogy with other forms in ''er-''; the Old Norse 1st person singular form was {{m|non|em}}.

====Verb====
{{head|is|verb form}}

# {{inflection of|is|vera||1|s|ind|pres}}
#: {{ux|is|{{l|is|ég|Ég}} '''er''' [[skemmtilegur]].|I '''am''' [[fun]] (masculine)}}
#: {{ux|is|[[hver|Hver]] '''er''' {{l|is|ég}}?|[[who|Who]] '''am''' I?}}
# {{inflection of|is|vera||3|s|ind|pres}}
#: {{ux|is|{{l|is|vita|Veit}} [[einhver]] [[hvar]] {{l|is|pabbi}} [[minn]] '''er'''?|[[does|Does]] [[anybody]] [[know]] [[where]] my [[dad]] '''is'''?}}
#: {{ux|is|[[hver|Hver]] '''er''' {{l|is|hann}}?|[[who|Who]] '''is''' [[he]]?}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|is|non|er}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*iz||he}}, from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*ís||he, that}}.

====Pronoun====
{{head|is|pronoun|cat2=relative pronouns}}

# {{lb|is|relative}} [[which]]
#: {{ux|is|{{l|is|maður|Maður}} {{l|is|vera|er}} [[sá]], '''er''' [[Jón]] [[heita|heitir]].|There [[is]] a [[man]] '''who''' is named [[John]].}}
#: {{ux|is|[[kona|Konan]], '''er''' {{l|is|hann}} {{l|is|vera|var}} að [[tala við]].|The [[woman]] to '''whom''' [[he]] [[was]] [[talk|talking]].}}
#: {{ux|is|[[þetta|Þetta]] {{l|is|vera|er}} [[borg|borgin]], '''er''' {{l|is|hann}} [[koma|kom]] [[frá]].|This is the [[city]] [[from]] '''which''' he [[originated]].}}
#: {{ux|is|[[bær|Bærinn]], '''er''' [[hún]] [[ætla]]r [[til]].|The [[town]] to '''which''' she's heading.}}
# {{lb|is|archaic}} in relations with a [[demonstrative pronoun]] ([[this]], [[that]], [[these]]) or [[personal pronoun]] ([[I]], [[we]], [[they]]), which represents the genitive of a [[relative pronoun]]
#: {{ux|is|Það er [[sá|sú]] bók, '''er''' {{l|is|maður|menn}} þekkja eigi [[höfundur|höfund]] hennar.|There is a book '''whose''' [[author]] people don't know.}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|is|conjunction}}

# {{lb|is|with an "[[indexical]]"; ''[[ábendingarorð]]''}} of a place, of a time
#* Judges 2:19
#*: {{quote|is|En '''er''' dómarinn andaðist, breyttu þeir að nýju verr en feður þeirra, með því að elta aðra guði til þess að þjóna þeim og falla fram fyrir þeim. Þeir létu eigi af gjörðum sínum né þrjóskubreytni sinni.|But '''when''' the judge died, the people returned to ways even more corrupt than those of their ancestors, following other gods and serving and worshiping them. They refused to give up their evil practices and stubborn ways.}}
#: {{ux|is|Þar '''er''' ég kom.|There '''whence''' I came.}}
#: {{ux|is|Þá '''er''' myndin var búin.|'''When''' the movie was finished.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|þá er þegar}}

===References===
* {{R:Zoega lite}}

