Often said to derive from {{m|is|ey||island}}, but perhaps more likely from {{der|is|non|ey||luck, fortune}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*awją}}.<ref>{{cite-book|is|title=Nöfn Íslendinga|author=Guðrún Kvaran|publisher=Forlagið|location=Reykjavík|year=2011|ISBN=978-9979-53-546-1}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|en|work=Nordic Names|author=Judith Ahrholdt|year=2004–2024|url=https://www.nordicnames.de/wiki/EY}}</ref>

===Proper noun===
{{is-proper noun|@@}}

# {{ng|suffix forming female given names}}
#: {{afex|is|lauf<t:leaf>|Laufey}}
#: {{afex|is|sól<t:sun>|Sóley}}
#: {{afex|is|sigur<t:victory>|Sigurey}}
#: {{afex|is|Þór<t:Thor>|Þórey}}

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|f.proper.j.acc+datju}}

===References===
<references />

-------- end text --------
