Page 3675 falla eins og flís við rass: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|to fit as tightly as a chip (metaphorically a thin, close cut) against the ass}}. This idiom is relatively recent in the Icelandic language with the oldest example in the {{m|is||Orðabók Háskólans's|the University Dictionary}} {{m|is||ritmálssafn|corpus of written language}} dating from the early 19th century from Guðmundur Jónsson's {{m|is||málsháttaasafn|corpus of idioms}}.

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|féll|féllu|fallið|11=eins og flís við rass|head=[[falla]] [[eins og]] [[flís]] [[við]] [[rass]]}}

# {{lb|is|idiomatic|simile|intransitive}} to [[fit like a glove]], to [[fit]] [[perfectly]]
#: {{ux|is|Þetta '''fellur eins og flís við rass'''.|This '''fits like a glove'''.}}

