Page 3923 fiðrildi: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|fiðrildi}} from the older term {{m|non|fífrildi}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*fifaldǭ}} {{m|gem-pro|*fīfildǭ||butterfly}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*pāpel-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*pe(i)pel-||butterfly}}. The term {{m|non|fiðrildi}} came through the [[folk etymology]] that it was related to the Old Norse word {{m|non|fiðri||feathers}} (compare the more modern {{cog|non|fiðr}}), from which the {{cog|is|fiður||feathers, down}} came.

Cognate with {{cog|goh|fīvaltra}} (> {{cog|gmh|viveltre}} > {{cog|de|Falter}}); {{cog|ang|fīfalde}} or {{m|ang|fifalde}}; {{cog|sv|fjäril}}; {{cog|no|fivrelde}} or {{m|no|fibrelde}} and {{cog|la|pāpiliō}}.

