Page 3935 fimbulvetur: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|fimbulvetr}}; from {{prefix|non|fimbul|t1=mighty, great|vetr|t2=winter|nocat=1}}. {{cog|nn|fimbulvetter}}, {{cog|fo|fimbulsvetur}}, {{cog|non-oen|fimbulvintr}} → {{cog|sv,da|fimbulvinter}} → {{cog|no|-}} {{m|nn|fimbulvinter}}. See English {{m|en|Fimbulwinter|fimbulwinter}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈfɪmpʏlˌvɛːtʏr/}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# A [[harsh]] [[winter]], the [[great]] and [[awful]] darkness preceding the [[Ragnarök|end of the world]] as written in the {{m|en|[[w:Prose Edda|Prose Edda]]||Younger Edda}}. It says three successive winters will come where snow and wind comes from all directions, without any intervening summer; during this time, there will be innumerable wars and ties of blood will no longer be respected: the next-of-kin will lay together and brothers will kill brothers.<ref>[http://www.snl.no/fimbulvinter ''Fimbulvinter'' (Store norske leksikon)]</ref> See ''[[w:Fimbulwinter|Fimbulwinter]]'' on Wikipedia.

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|@v}}

