Page 4118 fjöl-: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|fjǫl-}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*felu}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*pleh₁-}} (the Indo-European root is also the source of Ancient Greek {{m|grc|πολύς}}, Latin {{m|la|plus||more}}, Ossetian {{m|os|фыр||much}}, Old Irish {{m|sga|il}}, from whence the Welsh {{m|cy|lliaws}}). Cognate with {{cog|got|𐍆𐌹𐌻𐌿}}, {{cog|goh|filu||many}} (from which the German {{m|de|viel}} came), Old Saxon {{m|osx|filo}} and {{m|osx|filu}} (from which {{m|nds|veel||much}} came), English {{m|en|fele}} (Old English {{m|ang|fela||many, much}}). This adjective or prefix has been lost in English and modern Danish but is frequent in Icelandic; especially as a prefix in poetry but never as an independent adjective.

===Prefix===
{{head|is|prefix}}

# [[multi]], [[many]], [[much]], [[manifold]]

