Page 4360 foreldrar: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Once {{m|en|variants||''[[tvímyndir]]''; a different spelling, pronunciation, or form of the same word}} of {{m|is|foreldri||a parent}}.<ref name="arna">[http://www.arnastofnun.is/page/arnastofnun_ord_pistlar_foreldrar ''foreldrar — foreldri'']</ref> It is rare that a word's gender differs between grammatical numbers, but modern dictionaries generally list them as two distinct words — even though their form and declension is similar.<ref name="arna"/> The reason for this disparity in usage is the masculine word's lack of singular form.<ref name="arna"/>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈfɔːrɛltrar/}}
* {{audio|is|Is-foreldrar.oga}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|pluralonly}} [[parents]]; {{gloss|mother and father, or any combination thereof}} (''genealogical abbreviation'' '''[[for.]]''')

====Usage notes====
* The term is masculine when used in the plural but neuter when used in the singular {{m|is|foreldri||a parent}}.<ref name="arna"/><ref>[https://archive.is/20130702115053/bin.arnastofnun.is/leit.php?q=foreldrar ''foreldrar''] at [[w:is:Beygingarlýsing íslensks nútímamáls|Beygingarlýsing íslensks nútímamáls]]</ref> See there for singular declension.

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|m.pl}}

===References===
<references />
-------- end text --------
