Page 4523 framsóknardanska: -------- begin text --------
{{rfv|is|no cites}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|is|framsókn|danska}}. Presumably named after the Icelandic progressives ''([[framsóknarmenn]])'' that were pushing for Danish to be taught in Iceland. Icelanders became familiar with reading and writing in Danish, but lacked pronunciation skills, thus creating a form of Danish spoken with a lot of features of Icelandic pronunciation.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈfram.souhk.nar.tan.ska/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|anska|s=5}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|humorous}} The [[Danish]] language as spoken by [[Icelander]]s.
#: {{ux|is|Auðskildar voru aldrei mér enska, þýska og franska. En torskildust þó af tungum er töluð '''framsóknardanska'''.|t=English, German and French were never easy for me. But the most difficult of them is spoken framsóknardanska.}}

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|@d}}

