Page 4994 gamla settið: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|the old [[set]]}} (as in a cutlery set, furniture set, or TV set), as one's parents form a matching pair.
First seen on print in 1982.<ref>[https://timarit.is/page/978887?iabr=on#page/n26/mode/1up/search/%22gamla%20setti%C3%B0%22%20OR%20%22gamla%20settinu%22%20-%22sem%20hluta%22 Helgarpósturinn - 32. tölublað (13.08.1982). p. 27:] "Gamla settið hefur lært af fyrri reynslu og beitir henni."</ref><ref>[https://timarit.is/page/4018046?iabr=on#page/n26/mode/1up/search/%22gamla%20setti%C3%B0%22%20OR%20%22gamla%20settinu%22%20-%22sem%20hluta%22 Tíminn - 213. Tölublað - Blað 2 (19.09.1982). p. 27:] "nærtækasta skýringin er sennilega sú að unglingar vilja hræra aðeins upp í „gamla settinu“"</ref>

