Page 5328 gjörðu svo vel: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|is|gerðu svo vel||less common}}

===Etymology===
{{lit|do so well}}. ''Gjörðu'' is the [[imperative]] form of the archaic verb {{m|is|gjöra||to do}}. ''Gjöra'' is not used in modern Icelandic; instead it uses {{m|is|gera||to do}}.

The phrase ''gerðu svo vel'' can also be used but it is not as common, there it is derived from the modern verb {{m|is|gera||to do}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈcœ(r̥)sɔˌvɛːl/}}

===Phrase===
{{head|is|phrase|head=[[gjöra|gjörðu]] [[svo]] [[vel]]}}

# a polite expression when handing something to someone; [[here you go]]; [[there you go]]; [[my pleasure]]
#: {{ux|is|Gætirðu rétt mér [[salt|saltið]]?'' - ''Já, '''gjörðu svo vel'''.|Could you pass me the [[salt]]? - Sure, '''here you go'''.}}
# [[please]]
#: {{uxi|is|Næsti, '''gjörðu svo vel'''.|Next customer, '''please'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Viltu '''gjöra svo vel''' að hætta þessu?|Will you '''please''' stop that?!}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|verði þér að góðu||you're welcome}}

