Page 5462 gormur: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|is|2017|January|21}}
[[Image:Coil_spring.JPG|thumb|right|'''gormur''']]

===Etymology===
Attested since the 17th century. From an unattested {{inh|is|non|*gormr}}, whence also {{cog|nn|gorm}}, {{m|nn|gurm||mud, sludge}} and dialectal or obsolete {{cog|sv|gorm||filth; fish guts; fruit solids left over after pressing the juice out}}, from a {{inh|is|gem-pro|*gurmaz}}. Related to {{m|is|ger}} and {{m|is|gor}}. Ultimately from {{der|is|ine-pro|*gʷʰer-||hot}}. The meaning “coil, spring” developed from the resemblance of metal coils to fish or animal intestines.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/kɔrmʏr/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ɔrmʏr|s=2}}
* {{homophones|is|Gormur}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[mud]], [[sludge]]
# liquid animal [[faeces]]
# the [[guts]] or [[intestine]]s of a [[fish]]
# a bottomless [[morass]]
# a [[coil]] [[spring]] {{gloss|mechanical device}}
# [[coil]], [[spiral]], [[helix]], a coil-shaped object
# a coil of silver or gold [[wire]] for use in [[embroidery]]

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|m}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|mud|sludge}} {{l|is|leðja}}, {{l|is|drulla}}, {{l|is|korgur}}
* {{sense|guts, intestine}} {{l|is|innyfli}}, {{l|is|görn|garnir}}, {{l|is|þarmur|þarmar}}
* {{sense|spring}} {{l|is|fjöður}}
* {{sense|coil, spiral}} {{l|is|spírall}}

===References===
* {{R:is:Íslensk orðsifjabók|gormur}}
* {{R:svenska.se|saob|gorm}}
-------- end text --------
