Page 5625 grípa: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|grípa}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*grīpaną}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*gʰreyb-||to grasp, grab}}. Cognate with Norwegian {{m|nb|gripe}}, Swedish {{m|sv|gripa}}, Danish {{m|da|gribe}}, English {{m|en|gripe}}, Dutch {{m|nl|grijpen}}, German {{m|de|greifen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈkriːpa/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|iːpa|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|greip|gripu|gripið}}

# to [[catch]] an object
#: {{coi|is|að grípa bolta|to catch a ball (that has been thrown)}}
#: {{coi|is|að grípa á {{l|is|loft|lofti}}|to catch an object before it touches the ground}}
# to [[grab]], [[clasp]], [[grip]], [[grasp]]
#: {{uxi|is|Gríptu í höndina mína.|Grab my hand!}}
#: {{uxi|is|Hann {{l|is|grípa tækifæri|greip tækifærið}}.|He seized the opportunity.}}
# to catch someone in the act
#: {{coi|is|{{l|is|grípa glóðvolgan|grípa einhvern glóðvolgan}}|catch someone [[red-handed]]}}
# to [[arrest]] someone
# to [[grasp]] (understand)

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s1|gr|p}}

====Derived terms====
