Page 5638 gróa: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|Ri-verbs}}
{{wikipedia|Ri-sögn|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|gróa}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*grōaną}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*gʰreH₁-||to grow, become green}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|is|ouːa|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-ri|greri|11=gréri|gróið}}

# to [[grow]]
# to [[heal]]
#: {{ux|is|Sárið '''grær''' ekki.|The wound doesn't '''heal'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* One of the four [[w:is:Ri-sagnir|ri-verbs]] in Icelandic, the other being {{m|is|núa||to rub, massage; to wipe}}, {{m|is|snúa||to turn}} and {{m|is|róa||to row}}.
* As with the other ri-verbs, the past tense {{m|is||greri}} was originally pronounced with an ''e'' sound but is today pronounced with a ''[[é]]'' sound. There are therefore two spelling variants used: {{m|is||greri}} and {{m|is||gréri}}. The Icelandic Ministry of Education considers both variants to be equally correct,<ref>[https://ritreglur.arnastofnun.is/ Icelandic Ministry of Education - Announcements regarding orthography from 2016 and 2018, section 3.5.5]</ref> but many speakers consider the original {{m|is||greri}} spelling to be the more correct one.

====Conjugation====
{{rfinfl|is|verb}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|grow}} {{l|is|vaxa}}
* {{sense|heal}} {{l|is|[[verða]] [[heill]]}}

