Page 5777 gumi: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|gumi||a man|pos=''poetic''}} from the {{der|is|gem-pro|*gumô}}, originally from the {{der|is|ine-pro|*dʰǵʰm̥mō}}. {{cog|gem}} cognates include {{cog|osx|gumo}}, {{cog|goh|gumo}}, {{cog|no|gume}}, and {{cog|got|𐌲𐌿𐌼𐌰}}. The {{cog|ine}} root is also the source of {{cog|la|homo}} and {{cog|bat}} ''*žmo-'' ({{cog|lt|žmogus|žmōgùs}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈkʏːmɪ/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ʏːmɪ|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|poetic|in prose}} a [[man]]
#* ''Nú er sumar'' by [[w:Steingrímur Thorsteinsson|Steingrímur Thorsteinsson]]
#*: ''Nú er sumar,''
#*: ''gleðjist '''gumar''',''
#*: ''gaman er í dag.''
#*: ''Brosi veröld víða,''
#*: ''veðurlagsins blíða.''
#*: ''Eykur yndishag. Eykur yndishag.''

====Usage notes====
* Appears (scarcely) in prose for [[alliteration|alliterative]] purposes. The usual term for a man is {{m|is|maður}}.

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|((<m>,<m.plstem:gumn>))}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|guma}}

