Page 6166 háll: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|háll}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*hēlaz|t=slippery, deceitful}}, related to {{cog|gml|hāl||hidden}} and {{cog|goh|hāli||smooth, slippery, weak}}. Further etymology unsure:

* Maybe from the {{der|is|ine-pro|-}} root {{m|ine-pro|*ḱel-|t=to hide}} (compare {{cog|gem-pro|*helaną|t=to conceal, hide}}),

* or from {{m|ine-pro|*ḱelH-|t=to freeze}} (compare {{cog|sq|thjellët}})

* or from {{m|ine-pro|*kelH-|t=to incline}}.

Possible cognates in Icelandic are {{m|is|héla||hoarfrost}} and {{m|is|hagl||hail}}.<ref>{{R:ine:NIL|page=416}}</ref><ref>{{R:gem:EDPG|head=Hēli-}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈhautl/}}
* {{rhymes|is|autl|s=1}}

