===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# The [[High German]] dialects; the dialect continuum of German varieties stretching from the  highlands of southern Germany to Switzerland, Austria, and parts of France and Italy.
#: {{ux|is|Opinbert tungumál Lúxemborgar er í rauninni ekki þýska, heldur náskyld mállýska '''háþýsku''' sem kallast lúxemborgíska.|The official language of Luxembourg isn't actually German, but a closely related dialect of '''High German''' called Luxembourgish.}}
# The [[Standard German]] language; the standardised variety of German used in formal spoken and written settings throughout the German-speaking world.
#: {{syn|is|þýska|nútímaleg þýska}}
#: {{ux|is|Þó hann talaði hana reiprennandi var móðurmálið hans í rauninni ekki '''háþýska'''.|Although he spoke it fluently, his mother language wasn't actualyl '''High German'''.}}
# Classes which teach Standard German.
#: {{syn|is|þýska<qq:more common>}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég hata flesta tímana mína, en '''háþýska''' er skemmtileg.|I hate most of my classes, but '''High German''' is fun.}}

