Page 6710 hlakka: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|hlakka}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*hlakkōną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|is|ahka|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|hlakkaði|hlakkað}}

# to make the [[sound]] of an [[eagle]]
# used to show excitement, anticipation, or joy at the prospect of something
#: {{usex|is|Ég '''hlakka''' til jólanna!|I am '''excited''' for Christmas!}}

====Usage notes====
* This verb is used personally except in the phrase {{m|is|hlakka í}} where it is impersonal.
* The verb ''hlakka'' is one of several personal verbs—such as {{m|is|kvíða||to be anxious}}, {{m|is|finna||to feel, to sense}} and {{m|is|kenna|kenna til|to feel pain}}<ref name="os">[https://web.archive.org/web/20110722022107/http://old.ma.is/kenn/svp/kennsluefni/malfar/oper.htm Gott mál og vandað — nokkur vandmeðfarin atriði í daglegu máli] Ópersónulegar sagnir</ref>—that have come to be used impersonally (possibly since most impersonal Icelandic verbs denote feeling, the senses or some evaluation).<ref name="os"/> Because of this, using the subject in the accusative or dative instead of in the nominative is a common mistake:
*: <s>''Mig '''hlakkar''' til veislunnar.''</s>
*: <s>''Mér '''hlakkar''' til veislunnar.''</s>
*: ''Ég '''hlakka''' til veislunnar.''
*:: I '''look forward''' to the party.

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-w4|hl|a|kk|mp=-|pp=-}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|hlakka til|hlakka til einhvers|t=to [[look forward to]] something}}
* {{l|is|hlakka í|hlakka í einhverjum|t=for someone to feel giddy with joy}}
* {{l|is|hlakka yfir|hlakka yfir einhverju|t=to gloat over something}}

===References===
<references/>
-------- end text --------
