Page 6809 hnakki: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}
{{wikipedia|Hnakki (líffræði)|hnakki (the nape of the neck)|lang=is}}
{{wikipedia|Hnakki (tíska)|hnakki (fashion)|lang=is}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈn̥ahcɪ/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ahcɪ|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|hnakki}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*hnakkô}}.

Origin of the slang sense is uncertain. May be derived from the meat sense, in connection with {{m|is|skinka||ham}}, which is also used in a similar slang sense, or it may refer to the associated hairstyle (popular between 2005 and 2010) in which the only the hair of the back of the head points outwards.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[nape]] of the neck, back of the head
# [[shoulder]] {{gloss|meat behind an animals head, e.g. on a pig or fish}}
# {{lb|is|slang|pejorative}} a stereotypical grouping of [[superficial]] [[juvenile]]s associated with [[sport]], [[fitness]] and [[tan]]ning, that often [[bleach]] their hair and dress [[fashionably]], somewhat similar to a [[jock]]. Used primarily between 2005 and 2010.

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|m}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|is|emó}}, {{l|is|ímó||an emo}}
* {{l|is|gothari}}, {{l|is|goþþari}}, {{l|is|gottari||a goth}}
* {{l|is|nörd}}, {{l|is|nördi||a nerd, a geek}}
* {{l|is|pönkari||a punk}}
* {{l|is|skinka}}

===Etymology 2===
See {{m|is|hnakkur}}.

====Noun====
{{head|is|noun form|g=m}}

# {{inflection of|is|hnakkur||indef|dat|s}}

{{C|is|Anatomy}}

