Page 6857 hnjóta: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|gem-pro|*hneutaną}}, related to {{l|is|hnjótur}}, {{l|is|hnot}}, {{l|is|hnúta}}, and {{l|is|hnöggva}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈn̥jouːta/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ouːta|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|hnaut|hnutu|hnotið}}

# to [[stumble]] {{+obj|is|:um(acc)<over>}}
*: {{ux|is|Drengurinn '''hnaut''' um steininn.|The boy '''tripped over''' the rock.}}
** [[w:en:Stephan G. Stephansson|Stephan G. Stephansson]], ''Fullkomleikinn'' ("The Perfectness")
**: Hæsta takmark hugsjónar
**: haft í stiga aðeins var.
**: Að hnjóta um lífsins hála svið,
**: að hrasa og falla, en [[upp á við]],
**: er ferill framfara auði.
**:: Vision's highest goal
**:: was only kept in stairs.
**:: To '''trip over''' life's slippery stage,
**:: to stumble and fall, but [[upwards]],
**:: are the empty traces of progress.

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s2|hn|jó|t|mp=-}}

===References===
* {{R:Íslensk orðsifjabók 1989}}
-------- end text --------
