Page 7077 hrinda: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|hrinda}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*hrindaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈr̥ɪnta/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɪnta|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|hratt|hrundu|hrundið}} ''or''<br />
{{is-verb-weak|hrinti|hrint}}

# to [[push]], [[shove]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{ux|is|Hún '''hrinti''' mér!|She '''pushed''' me!}}
#: {{ux|is|Áhöld eru um hvort Gunnar hafi dottið niður stigann eða honum verið '''hrint'''.|It is debated whether Gunnar fell down the stairs or was '''pushed'''.}}
# {{lb|is|figuratively}} to [[get]] something [[going]], to [[push]] into action, often used in set phrases such as {{m|is|hrinda í framkvæmd||to put into effect}} or {{m|is|hrinda af stað||to start}}. {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{ux|is|Í maí var verkinu loks '''hrundið''' í framkvæmd.|The project was finally '''started''' in May.}}
#: {{ux|is|Að '''hrinda''' af stað byltingu.|To '''start''' a revolution.}}
#: {{ux|is|Að '''hrinda''' af stað fyrirtæki.|To '''start''' a company.}}

====Usage notes====
The strong conjugation is mostly used for sense 2. Moreover, weak forms are now always used in the present tense and the original strong forms in singular present indicative (''hrind'', ''hrindur'') are obsolete.

====Conjugation====
Strong conjugation:
{{is-conj-s3|hr|i|nd}}
Weak conjugation:
{{is-conj-w2|hr|i|nd}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|hrinda í framkvæmd||to put something into effect}}
* {{l|is|hrinda af stað||to start}} (synonym {{l|is|koma af stað}})
* {{l|is|hrinda árás||to repel an attack}}
* {{l|is|hrinda frá sér vatni||to be water-repellent, to repel water}}

-------- end text --------
