Page 7079 hringaná: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{com|is|hringur|alt1=hringar|t1=rings (jewellery)|Ná}}, an alternative spelling of {{m|is|Gná}}, the name of a Norse goddess.
Jewellery is often utilized when creating {{w|kenning|kennings}} about women.

Only used in {{w|Jónas Hallgrímsson}}'s poem {{m|is|Hættu að gráta hringaná}}, the title thus meaning "Don't cry, dear girl".

