===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|is|non|hrífa||to grip, snatch}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*hrībaną||to grip, snatch}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*(s)kreybʰ-||to scratch}}. Has become conflated with {{der|is|gem-pro|*rīfaną}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*h₁reyp-||to tear}}, in each subsequent daughter language, cf. {{cog|ang|gehrīfnian||to become fierce, rapacious}} and {{cog|ofs|hrīva||to tear}}. Ultimately the sense is 'to make an impression on'.

