Page 7529 höfrungur: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Earliest attested in 16th century. No cognates in related languages, Faroese has already adopted ''dolfin''. Asgeir Blöndal Magnusson estimates correlation with ''-hafur'' (Old English ''hæfer'', Latin ''caper'') comparing the leaps of the dolphin to those of the goat. Doubtful.
Perhaps simply from ''haf'' ("sea") and ''ungur,'' that is, Hefring, a Norwegian mountain butting into the sea; and Hefring, daughter of Ægir the sea spirit.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈhœvruŋkʏr/}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[dolphin]]; specifically the [[common dolphin]] ({{taxfmt|Delphinus delphis|species}})

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|m}}

====Synonyms====
