Page 7724 í kjölfar: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Analogous to the English {{m|en|in the wake of}} – a [[wake]] always follows a ship. Compare Danish {{m|da|kølvand|i kølvandet på}} and Norwegian {{m|nb|kjølvann|i kjølvannet av}}.

===Prepositional phrase===
{{head|is|prepositional phrase}}

# {{lb|is|idiomatic}} [[in the wake of]], [[following]], shortly after, [[subsequently]] {{gloss|an event that follows a related event}}
#: {{uxi|is|Hann var [[handtaka|handtekinn]] og [[ákæra|ákærður]] '''í kjölfarið'''.|He was arrested and [[subsequently]] charged.}}
# {{lb|is|idiomatic}} [[in the wake of]], to occur as a [[result]], to [[accompany]], [[bring about|brought about by]]
#: {{syn|is|afleiðing|vegna}}
#: {{uxi|is|Það flæddi mikið '''í kjölfar''' fellibylsins.|Significant flooding occurred as a result of the hurricane.}}

====Usage notes====
Often as "'''''[[koma]]''' í kjölfarið''" or "'''''[[fylgja]]''' í kjölfarið''".

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|fylgifiskur}}
