{{is-proper noun|@@}}

# [[Jesus]]

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|m.stem:Jesú.acc-:m[archaic or Biblical].dat+gen-}}

Note: this declension, highly irregular and unique in Icelandic, is taken directly from the Latin declension (see the Latin entry {{m|la|Iēsus}}). Originally, the accusative was always ''Jesúm'', but in recent times it is more commonly ''Jesú'', under influence from the other case forms. Also note the distinct vocative form, ''Jesú'', whereas for other Icelandic words the nominative form is normally used in vocative constructions.

