# The “[[Christmas]] [[book]] [[flood]]”; the [[multitude]] of books (especially newly published books) available in shops in the weeks before Christmas in Iceland, where most new books are published at this time of year.
#* {{quote-journal
|is
|author=Árni Hallgrímsson
|editor=Árni Hallgrímsson
|title=Bækur
|trans-title=Books
|journal=Iðunn
|url=http://timarit.is/view_page_init.jsp?gegnirId=000511753
|location=Reykjavík
|year=1936
|volume=XIX
|issue=3–4
|page=386
|pageurl=http://timarit.is/view_page_init.jsp?pageId=4849087
|passage=Það getur vel verið, að þessi gráa og látlausa hversdagssaga drukkni í '''jólabókaflóðinu''' í ár.
|translation=It may well be that this gray and unassuming everyday story will drown in this year’s '''Christmas book flood'''.
}}
#* {{quote-journal
|is
|title=Dagbók
|trans-title=Diary/Journal
|journal=Morgunblaðið
|url=http://timarit.is/view_page_init.jsp?issId=106223&pageId=1250456
|location=Reykjavík
|date=1943-12-21
|volume=30
|issue=289
|page=10
|pageurl=http://timarit.is/view_page_init.jsp?issId=106223&pageId=1250456
|passage=Í hinu mikla '''jólabókaflóði''' er lítið og laglegt hefti með snotri mynd framan á, sem heitir: „Jeg skal segja þjer“
|translation=In the great '''Christmas book flood''' there is a small and pretty booklet with a pretty picture on the cover, entitled: “I shall tell you”
}}
#* {{quote-journal
|is
|title=Ástarsögur hverfa af jólabókamarkaði
|trans-title=Love stories disappear from Christmas book market
