Page 7999 jólakaka: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|Christmas cake}}, a name which was used to refer to {{w|fruitcake|fruitcakes}} which were once (but not anymore) often served during Christmas in Iceland.<ref>[https://timarit.is/page/1952978 Hvað er jólakaka? Morgunblaðið, 1999-12-02, p. 57.]</ref> The name may have carried over to raisin pound cakes since they look somewhat similar and include raisins.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[raisin]] [[pound cake]]
# {{lb|is|obsolete|_|unless when used with the clarifier “{{l|is||[[enskur|ensk]] jólakaka}}”}} [[fruit cake]]
#: {{syn|is|ávaxtakaka}}
# {{lb|is|when describing foreign customs}} any cake typically served during Christmas

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|@kak}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|sandkaka||pound cake}}
* {{l|is|bla bla jólakaka}}

