Page 8241 kasmekktur: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Coined by the Icelandic author [[w:Halldór Laxness|Halldór Laxness]] from the epic novel ''[[w:en:Independent People|Sjálfstætt fólk]]'' ("Independent People") when describing weather conditions. From {{af|is|[[kös|kas-]]<t:heap>|mekktur<t:with a mane>}}, from the noun {{m|is|makki||mane}}.<ref>{{webofscience|7039|Hvað er þetta 'kas' þegar konur eru kasólettar?|What does the ''kas'' in ''kasólettur'' mean?}}</ref>

===Adjective===
{{head|is|adjective|g=m|feminine|kasmekkt|neuter|kasmekkt}}

# probably signifying a [[thick]] [[heap]] of [[cloud]]s, reminiscent of a horse's [[mane]]
#* ''[[w:en:Independent People|Sjálfstætt fólk]]'' ("Independent People") by [[w:Halldór Laxness|Halldór Laxness]]
#*: {{quote|is|Hann var '''kasmekktur''' á Bláfjöll, með brunagaddi og hægu skafroki, fé á innistöðu.|He was '''thick clouded''' at Bláfjöll, with a very strong frost and drifting winds, and livestock in the house.}}

====References====
<references/>
-------- end text --------
