===Etymology===
The word {{m|is|klám}} is considered to be related to the Norwegian word {{m|no|klam||moist, glutinous, adhesive}}. Compare the {{cog|grc|-}} words {{m|grc|γλάμη}}, {{m|grc|γλάμον}}, {{m|grc|γλαμυρός}} and the Lithuanian word {{m|lt|glemes|t=slime}}. The word {{m|is|klám}} is also connected to the Low German word {{m|de|klam}}.<ref>{{webofscience|434|Hver er uppruni orðsins klám?|Where does the word ''klám'' come from?}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/kʰlauːm/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|auːm|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[porn]], [[pornography]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég fann '''klám''' á tölvunni hennar.|I found '''porn''' on her computer.}}

