Page 9104 kvíða: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈkʰviːða/}}
** {{rhymes|is|iːða}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|kvíða}}. Possibly related to {{m+|ang|cwīðan}} and {{m+|osx|qwiðean|t=to complain}}.<ref>{{R:gem:Seebold|head=KWEIÞ-*A-|page=313}}</ref>

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|kveið|kviðu|kviðið}}

# to be [[anxious]] or [[apprehensive]] about {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''kvíði''' engu.|I'm not nervous about anything.}}

====Usage notes====
Formerly a weak verb (past tense ''kvíddi'', supine ''kvítt''), it has adopted the strong declension of verbs like {{m|is|bíða}}, {{m|is|ríða}}, {{m|is|líða}} and now only follows the weak declension in the present tense (''ég kvíði'', ''þú kvíðir''), although there too strong forms (''ég kvíð'', ''þú kvíður'') are also found.<ref>{{R:is:BÍN}}</ref>

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj_(kvíða)|mp=-|pp=-}}

====Related terms====
