Page 9234 Köben: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|is|Køben}}

===Etymology===
Shortening of {{bor|is|da|København}}.

===Proper noun===
{{head|is|proper noun}}

# {{lb|is|informal}} {{place|is|capital city|c/Denmark|t=Copenhagen}}
#: {{uxi|is|Það eru ódýr flug til '''Köben''' þessa dagana.|There are some cheap flights available to '''Copenhagen''' these days.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Kallinn loksins mættur til '''kóngsins Köben'''.|I have finally made it to '''Copenhagen, the king's city'''!}}

====Usage notes====
This form is extremely common in colloquial speech; for many speakers it is more common than the full name {{m|is|Kaupmannahöfn}}. "Kóngsins Köben" is also a term that is commonly seen, but it is much more [[jocular]]; it refers to Copenhagen being the residence of Iceland's former king. The Icelandic usage of "Köben" is considered extremely silly by Danish people, while it is a neutral term in Iceland.

====Declension====
{{rfinfl|is|proper noun}}
