Page 9330 lang-: -------- begin text --------

===Prefix===
{{head|is|prefix}}

# [[by far]], [[absolute]]
#: {{ux|is|Þú ert '''lang'''besti bróðir minn!|You're my best brother '''ever'''!}}
#: {{ux|is|Rakel kom með '''lang'''besta svarið.|Rakel's answer is '''by far''' the best.}}
# [[long]]
#: {{ux|is|'''Lang'''korna hrísgrjón.|'''Long'''-grain rice.}}
# [[long]], [[far]], [[distant]]

====Usage notes====
* Writing compound terms prefixed with {{m|is|lang-}} as [[hyphen]]ated is allowed (along with {{m|is|hálf-}}, {{m|is|jafn-}} and {{m|is|all-}}):<ref>[http://www.rthj.hi.is/solofile/1011143 XIII. Bandstrik] ("hyphens")</ref>
*: ''Þetta er '''lang'''-stærsti foss landsins.''
*:: This is '''by far''' the largest waterfall in the country.

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|is}}

===References===
<references />
-------- end text --------
Page 9331 langa: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈlauŋka/|[ˈlɐwŋkɐ]}}
*: {{rhymes|is|auŋka|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|langa|t=to long for; desire}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*langōną|t=to desire; long for}}, related to {{cog|en|long}}, {{cog|de|verlangen}}. More at {{l|en|long}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|langaði|langað}}

# {{lb|is|impersonal}} to [[want]]
#: {{ux|is|Hvað '''langar''' þig í? — Mig '''langar''' í nammi og ís!|What do you '''want'''? — I '''want''' candy and ice cream!}}
#: {{uxi|is|Mig '''langar''' heim.|I '''want''' to go home.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Hana '''langaði''' að hitta foreldra mína.|She '''wanted''' to meet my parents.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The person who wants to do something is in the accusative case and the verb is conjugated in the third-person singular. When you are referring to an object you want, {{m|is|langa í|t=to want, to have an appetite for something}} is used. When you want to perform a [[verb]], the verb '''''langa''''' is used.

=====Derived terms=====
{{der2|is
|langa í
|langa til}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|is|non|langa}}; compare {{cog|fo|longa}}.

