Page 9476 leggja á: -------- begin text --------

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|lagði|lagt|11=á}}

# to [[hang up]] {{+obj|is|&intransitive/acc}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég tók upp símann, sagði „ég er á leiðinni“ og '''laggði''' svo '''á'''.|I picked up the phone and said "I'm on my way" and then '''hung up'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* The verb {{m|is|skella á}} has a harsher and more of a negative connotation (akin to ''slamming'' the phone down) than the verb {{m|is|leggja á}} which has a softer meaning (akin to ''laying'' the phone down).

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|hang up}} {{l|is|skella á}}

{{cln|is|ambitransitive verbs}}
-------- end text --------
Page 9477 leggja á minnið: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|to put on the memory}}.

===Noun===
{{is-verb-weak|lagði|lagt|11=á minnið}}

# to [[keep]] in [[mind]], to [[memorise]], to [[study]], to [[learn]] {{+obj|is|acc}}
#: {{ux|is|Allir þurfa að '''leggja''' reglurnar '''á minnið'''.|Everybody needs to '''memorise''' the rules.}}

====Usage notes====
* The thing or object which is being ''memorised'' or ''kept in mind'' is used between {{m|is|leggja}} and {{m|is||á minnið|on memory}} in the accusative form:
*: ''Við þurfum að '''leggja''' alla bókina '''á minnið''' fyrir prófið!''
*:: We need to '''memorise''' the whole book for the test.
