# [[interrupted clubmoss]] ({{taxlink|Lycopodium annotinum|species}})
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1954|title=Nokkrir fundarstaðir fágætra jurta|journal=Náttúrufræðingurinn|trans-title=Some discovery sites of rare plants|trans-journal=The Natural Scientist|author=Ingólfur Davíðsson|volume=24|issue=1|page=31–36|passage=''Í berghlaupinu mikla (hólahrúgaldinu) utan við Stakkahlíð vex allmikið af '''lyngjafna''' (Lycopodium annotinum), einkum nálægt ánni á Hraundal.''|translation=In the large rock slide (the formless hill) outside Stakkahlíð grows a considerable amount of '''interrupted clubmoss''' (Lycopodium annotinum), especially close to the river at Hraundalur.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1995|title=Karrar og gróðurfar|trans-title=Rock ptarmigans and flora|journal=Náttúrufræðingurinn|trans-journal=The Natural Scientist|author=Ólafur Karl Nielsen|volume=65|issue=1-2|page=81–102|passage=''Ekki var greint á milli litunarjafna ''Diphazium alpinum'', '''lyngjafna''' ''Lycopodium annotinum'', mosajafna ''Selaginella selaginoides'' og skollafingurs ''Huperzia selago''.''|translation=No distinction was made between alpine clubmoss ''Dyphazium alpinum'', '''interrupted clubmoss''' ''Lycopodium annotinum'', lesser clubmoss ''Selaginella selaginoides'' and fir clubmoss ''Huperzia selago''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=2007|journal=Læknablaðið|trans-journal=The Medical Journal|title=Alkalóíðar úr íslenskum jafnategundum (Lycopodium), andkólínesterasaverkun in vitro|trans-title=Alkaloids from Icelandic clubmoss species (Lycopodium), anticholinesterase effect in vitro|author=Elsa Steinunn Halldórsdóttir|volume=93|issue=Supplement 53|page=33|passage=''Einangraðir voru þrír alkalóíðar úr '''lyngjafna''' og reyndust þeir vera annotinin, annotin og annotin N-oxíð.''|translation=Three alkaloids from the '''interrupted clubmoss''' were isolated and they turned out to be annotinine, annotine and annotine N-oxide.}}

