Page 10158 maður er manns gaman: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|is|2015|January|21}}

===Etymology===
{{lit|person is person’s joy}}. (Antonymic is the sentiment of the {{cog|la|-}} expression {{m|la|homō hominī lupus||man is a wolf to man}}.) Compare {{cog|nn|mann er manns gaman}}.

The proverb is from the forty-seventh verse of the ''[[w:Hávamál|Hávamál]]'', one of the books of the ''[[w:Poetic Edda|Poetic Edda]]''.<ref name="vísinda">{{webofscience|6310|Hvað þýðir "maður er manns gaman"?|What does ''maður er manns gaman'' mean?}}</ref>

{{rel-top5|the 47th verse of the Hávamál}}
* ''[[w:Hávamál|Hávamál]]'' verse 47 in Old Norse<ref name="vísinda"/>
*: Ungr var ek forðum
*: fór ek einn saman
*: þá varð ek villr vega;
*: auðigr þóttumk
*: er ek annan fann
*: '''maðr er manns gaman'''.
* English translation by [[w:Benjamin Thorpe|Benjamin Thorpe]]<ref>{{cite-web|title=Archived copy|url=http://www.northvegr.org/lore/poetic2/006_03.php|accessdate=4 October 2008|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20080514023731/http://www.northvegr.org/lore/poetic2/006_03.php|archivedate=14 May 2008}}</ref>
*: I was once young,
*: I was journeying alone,
*: and lost my way;
*: rich I thought myself,
*: when I met another.
*: '''Man is the joy of man'''.
* English translation by Henry A. Bellows<ref>[http://www.sacred-texts.com/neu/poe/poe04.htm]</ref>
*: Young was I once,
*: and wandered alone,
*: And nought of the road I knew;
*: Rich did I feel
*: when a comrade I found,
*: for '''man is man's delight'''.
* English translation by Olive Bray <ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20081017055412/http://www.anomy.net/havamal/]; ''The Elder or Poetic Edda'', edited and translated by Olive Bray (London: Printed for the Viking Club, 1908), pages 61-111</ref>
*: Young was I once,
*: I walked alone,
*: and bewildered seemed in the way;
*: then I found me another
*: and rich I thought me,
*: for '''man is the joy of man'''.
* English translation by [[w:W. H. Auden|W. H. Auden]] and P. B. Taylor<ref>{{cite-web|url=http://www.anomy.net/havamal/|title=Archived copy|accessdate=4 October 2008|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20081017055412/http://www.anomy.net/havamal/|archivedate=17 October 2008}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|title=Archived copy|url=http://vta.gamall-steinn.org/havamal.htm|accessdate=4 October 2008|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20050912100548/http://vta.gamall-steinn.org/havamal.htm|archivedate=12 September 2005}}</ref>
*: Young and alone
*: on a long road,
*: Once I lost my way:
*: Rich I felt
*: when I found another;
*: '''Man rejoices in man'''.
{{rel-bottom}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈmaːðʏr ɛ(ː)r ˈmanːs ˈkaːman/}}

===Proverb===
{{head|is|proverb}}

# people enjoy the company of other people
#* [[w:Rune Poems|Icelandic Rune Poem]], found in manuscript AM 461 12mo ([https://www.ragweedforge.com/rpin.html], [https://www.ragweedforge.com/rpie.html]):
#*: Maðr
#*: er manns gaman
#*: ok moldar auki
#*: ok skipa skreytir.
#*: homo mildingr.
#*:: Man
#*:: delight of man
#*:: and augmentation of the earth
#*:: and adorner of ships.

