Page 10281 margur verður af aurum api: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|many become a monkey from money|money makes monkeys out of men}}.<ref name="vísinda">{{webofscience|1857|Í Hávamálum er sagt að margur verði af aurum api. Hefur höfundurinn vitað hvað api var?|It is written in ''Hávamál'' that money makes monkeys out of men. Did the author actually know of monkeys?}}</ref>

The proverb is a reference to (quotation of) the seventh-fifth verse of the ''[[w:Hávamál|Hávamál]]'', one of the books of the ''[[w:Poetic Edda|Poetic Edda]]''.

{{rel-top5|the 75th verse of the Hávamál}}
* ''[[w:Hávamál|Hávamál]]'' verse 47 in updated (Icelandic) spelling<ref name="vísinda"/>
*: Veit-a hinn
*: er vætki veit:
*: '''Margur verður af aurum api.'''
*: Maður er auðigur,
*: annar óauðigur,
*: skyli-t þann vítka vár.
* English translation by [[w:Benjamin Thorpe|Benjamin Thorpe]]<ref>{{cite-web|title=Archived copy|url=http://www.northvegr.org/lore/poetic2/006_04.php|accessdate=8 October 2009|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20091027034146/http://www.northvegr.org/lore/poetic2/006_04.php|archivedate=27 October 2009}}</ref>
*: He (only) knows not
*: who knows nothing,
*: that '''many a one apes another'''.
*: One man is rich,
*: another poor:
*: let him not be thought blameworthy.
* English translation by Henry A. Bellows<ref>[http://www.sacred-texts.com/neu/poe/poe04.htm]</ref>
*: A man knows not,
*: if nothing he knows,
*: '''That gold oft apes begets''';
*: One man is wealthy
*: and one is poor,
*: Yet scorn for him none should know.
* English translation by Olive Bray <ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20081017055412/http://www.anomy.net/havamal/]; ''The Elder or Poetic Edda'', edited and translated by Olive Bray (London: Printed for the Viking Club, 1908), pages 61-111</ref>
*: He that learns nought will never know
*: '''how one is the fool of another''',
*: for if one be rich another is poor
*: and for that should bear no blame.
* English translation by [[w:W. H. Auden|W. H. Auden]] and P. B. Taylor<ref>{{cite-web|url=http://www.anomy.net/havamal/|title=Archived copy|accessdate=8 October 2009|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20081017055412/http://www.anomy.net/havamal/|archivedate=17 October 2008}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|title=Archived copy|url=http://vta.gamall-steinn.org/havamal.htm|accessdate=8 October 2009|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20050912100548/http://vta.gamall-steinn.org/havamal.htm|archivedate=12 September 2005}}</ref>
*: The half wit does not know that '''gold'''
*: '''Makes apes of many men''':
*: One is rich, one is poor,
*: There is no blame in that.
{{rel-bottom}}

===Proverb===
