Page 10447 með lögum skal land byggja: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|with laws shall land be built|land shall be built by laws}}.
The phrase is the opening words of the preamble to [[Jyske Lov]] (Law of Jutland) issued 1241 by King Valdemar II in Vordingborg.

Compare {{cog|gmq-oda|mæth logh skal land byggiæs}}, {{cog|da|med lov skal land bygges}}, {{cog|fo|við lóg skal land byggjast}}, {{cog|no|med Lov skal Landet byggjast}}, {{cog|sv|land skall med lag byggas}}, {{m|sv|med lag skall land byggas}}.

===Phrase===
{{head|is|phrase|head=[[með]] [[lög]]um [[skulu|skal]] [[land]] [[byggja]]}}

# "a country shall be built by [[law]]s", "the land will be built by laws", "with laws shall we build the land", the motto of [[w:en:Shetland Islands Council|Shetland Islands Council]], [[w:en:Víkingasveitin|Víkingasveitin]] and the [[w:en:Icelandic Police|Icelandic Police]]

====See also====
* In [[w:en:Njáls saga|Njáls saga]] the proverb {{m|is|með lögum skal land byggja en með ólögum eyða||land shall be built by laws, but desolated without them; with laws shall land be built, but desolated without laws}} appears. In the [[w:en:Frostathing Law|Frostathing Law]] the passage {{m|is|at lögum skal land várt byggja en eigi at ulögum øyða||our land shall be built on laws and not desolated with lawlessness}} appears. (Note, ólög can also represent bad laws, or laws that are not in harmony).
-------- end text --------
Page 10448 meðal: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|meðal}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*midlą|t=middle}}. Compare {{cog|da|middel|t=means, something used to cure}}, which was instead probably borrowed through Low German.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈmɛːðal/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɛːðal}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# a [[medicine]], a [[drug]]
# {{lb|is|archaic}} [[means]]
#: ''[[tilgangurinn helgar meðalið|Tilgangurinn helgar '''meðalið'''.]]''
#:: [[the end justifies the means|The end justifies the '''means'''.]]

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|n.uUmut[traditional, prescribed],umut[also common]}}

