Page 10521 mellufær: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{com|is|mella|fær|t1=whore|t2=capable}}, probably originally in the meaning of "to speak a language well enough to be able to request the services of prostitutes" rather than "to be as capable as a whore". Today the word however only means "minimally capable" and usually does not evoke imagery of prostitution to listeners.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈmɛtlʏˌfaiːr/}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|-}}

# {{lb|is|informal}} to have some minimum necessary amount of knowledge in a foreign language to be able to communicate effectively
#: {{uxi|is|Æ, ég er svona mellufær í þýsku.|Well, I can communicate in German.}}
# {{lb|is|informal|by extension of the above}} to have some minimum necessary amount of skill to be able to do something effectively
#: {{uxi|is|Hann er mellufær á trommur.|He can play the drums, but he's not exactly an advanced player.}}

====Declension====
{{is-decl-adj-1|melluf|æ|r|comp=-}}
-------- end text --------
