Page 10659 minn: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|mínn}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*mīnaz}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*méynos}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/mɪnː/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɪnː|s=1}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun|feminine|mín|neuter|mitt}}

# {{lb|is|possessive}} [[my]], [[mine]] (used referring to someone/something masculine)
#* '''1928''', [[w:is:Krummavísa|Krummavísa]] (“Raven Song”, on the [[w:source:Krummavísa|Icelandic Wikisource]]) by [[w:is:Jón Ásgeirsson|Jón Ásgeirsson]]
#*: {{quote|is|''Krummi krunkar úti,''<br>''kallar á nafna sinn:''<br>''„Ég fann höfud af hrúti''<br>''hrygg og gæruskinn.“''<br>''Komdu nú og kroppaðu með mér,''<br>''krummi nafni '''minn'''.''
|translation=“Krummi croaks outside,<br>calling his namesake:<br>‘I found the head of a ram,<br>backbone and sheepskin.’<br>Come now and peck with me,<br>Krummi, '''my''' namesake.”}}
#* ''Á Sprengisandi'' (“On Sprengisandur”) by [[w:en:Grímur Thomsen|Grímur Thomsen]]
#*: Ríðum, ríðum og rekum yfir sandinn,
#*: rennur sól á bak við Arnarfell,
#*: hér á reiki er margur óhreinn andinn,
#*: úr því fer að skyggja á jökulsvell;
#*: Drottinn leiði drösulinn '''minn''',
#*: drjúgur verður síðasti áfanginn.
#*:: Ride, ride, ride hard across the sands,
#*:: the sun is settling behind Arnarfell.
#*:: Here many spirits of the dark
#*:: threaten in the gloom over the glacier's ice.
#*:: The Lord leads '''my''' horse,
#*:: it is still a long, long way home.
#: {{ux|is|Þetta er maðurinn '''minn''', hann Þorlákur.|This is '''my''' husband Þorlákur.}}

====Declension====
{{is-decl-pron-minn}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|dömur mínar og herrar}}
* {{l|is|mínlegur}}
* {{l|is|minns||the miniaturized character I'm playing as}}

{{cln|is|possessive pronouns}}

-------- end text --------
