Page 10751 mjöður: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|mjǫðr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*meduz}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*médʰu||sweet drink}}.

''Germanic cognates:'' Old Frisian {{m|ofs|mede}}, Middle Low German {{m|gml|mēde}}, Dutch {{m|nl|mede}}, Old High German {{m|goh|meto}} (German {{m|de|Met}}) and Old English {{m|ang|medu}} (whence {{m|en|mead}}).

''Indo-European cognates:'' Sanskrit {{m|sa|मधु}}, Ancient Greek {{m|grc|μέθυ||wine}}, Latin {{m|la|medus}}, Old Irish {{m|sga|mid}}, Welsh {{m|cy|medd||mead}}, Old Church Slavonic {{m|cu|медъ||honey}}, Ukrainian {{m|uk|мед||honey}}, Russian {{m|ru|мёд||honey, mead}}, Lithuanian {{m|lt|medùs||honey}}, Tocharian B {{m|txb|mīt}}.

Compare also Finnish and Estonian {{m|fi|mesi}} and the Hungarian {{m|hu|méz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈmjœːðʏr/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|œːðʏr|s=2}}

===Noun===
