Page 10839 Mónakó: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|is|grc|μόνοικος||single house}}, from {{m|grc|μόνος||single, alone}} + {{m|grc|οἶκος||house}}, the name of the 6th century BC colony of [[Phocaeans]] and an epithet of [[Heracles]] (Hercules), ''Ἡρακλῆς Μόνοικος'' {{qualifier|Heracles Monoikos}}. According to an ancient Greek [[myth]] and a [[Ligurian]] [[legend]], Heracles passed through the Monaco area. A temple was constructed there by Phocaeans, the temple of ''Heracles Monoikos'' (Strabo, Geography, Gaul, 4.6.3).

===Proper noun===
{{head|is|proper noun|g=n}}

