Page 10921 mylla: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Alteration of earlier {{m|is|mylna}}, likely influenced by the Danish cognate {{m|da|mølle}}. The earlier form {{l|is||mylna}} is likely borrowed from {{der|is|ang|mylen}}, or from {{der|is|osx|mulin}}, in either case from {{der|is|gmw-pro|*mulīnu|t=mill}}, from {{der|is|LL.|molīna}}, from {{der|is|la|molō|t=grind, mill|pos=verb}}. Ultimately from {{der|is|ine-pro|*melh₂-|t=grind, crush}} and related to several inherited words such as {{m|is|mala}}, {{m|is|mylja}} and {{m|is|mold}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈmɪlːa/}}
*: {{audio|is|Is-mylla.oga}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɪlːa|s=2}}
*: Homophones: {{l|is|milla}}

