From {{inh|is|non|Mǫrðr}}, from {{m|is|mǫrðr||marten}} (modern Icelandic {{m|is|mörður}}), from {{der|is|gem-pro|*marþuz}}. It remained in use as a personal name in Iceland until at least the 13th century, but then acquired negative connotations due to the treacherous conduct of Mǫrðr Valgarðsson (born circa 969) related in the ''[[w:Njáls saga|Njáls saga]]'', whereafter it fell into disuse. It was revived in the 20th century. The first bearer after revival was born in 1902, but bore it as a second name. The second bearer, and the first to bear it as a first (and only) given name, is [[parliamentarian]] [[w:Mörður Árnason|Mörður Árnason]], born in 1953.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈmœrðʏr/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|œrðʏr|s=2}}
*: Homophones: {{l|is|mörður}}

===Proper noun===
{{is-proper noun|@@}}

# {{given name|is|male}}

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|m,ar.unumut.imut}}
-------- end text --------
Page 11007 mörgæs: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|is|2018|June|16}}
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|is|mör|t1=suet|gæs|t2=goose}}, a partial calque based on the supposed derivation of {{m|en|penguin}} from {{cog|la|pinguis||fat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈmœr.caiːs/}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[penguin]]
#: {{ux|is|'''Mörgæsir''' eru sætar.|'''Penguins''' are cute.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|date=2 May 1883|journal=Norðanfari|volume=22|issue=21-22|page=47|title=Fá orð um ferðir fugla|trans-title=A few words about the journeys of birds|url=http://timarit.is/view_page_init.jsp?issId=139320&pageId=2041672&lang=is&q=M%F6rg%E6sir|passage=''Þar dvelja '''mörgæsirnar''' hina 6 vetrarmánuði og hljóta sífellt að berjast við storm og ís, er hvorttveggja hlýtur að skerða ró og ánægju fuglsins.''|translation=The '''penguins''' stay there those 6 winter months and must continually contend with storm and ice, when both must negatively affect the tranquility and enjoyment of the bird.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1979|journal=Dýraverndarinn|volume=65|issue=3-4|page=16|title=Eintal í dýragarðinum|trans-title=Soliloquy in the zoo|url=http://timarit.is/view_page_init.jsp?issId=316355&pageId=4949400&lang=is&q=m%F6rg%E6sar|passage=''Eggin eru mjög oft ófrjó, og ef þau klekjast ekki út, leggst hin vonsvikna móðir á egg annarar '''mörgæsar'''.''|translation=The eggs are very often infertile, and if they fail to hatch, the disappointed mother sits on the egg of another '''penguin'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1991|journal=Náttúrufræðingurinn|volume=61|issue=1|page=21|title=Fuglalíf á Falklandseyjum|trans-title=Birdlife on the Falkland Islands|url=http://timarit.is/view_page_init.jsp?issId=291219&pageId=4272974&lang=is&q=m%F6rg%E6sir|passage=''Skemmtilegast er að heimsækja '''mörgæsa'''byggðirnar enda eru engar '''mörgæsir''' fyrir norðan miðbaug.''|translation=The most interesting [thing] is visiting the '''penguin''' settlements, since there are no '''penguins''' north of the equator.}}

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|f}}

{{C|is|Birds}}
-------- end text --------
