Page 11029 nafnháttarmerki: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=is}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|is|nhm.||abbreviation}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|is|nafnháttar|merki}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈnapn.hauh.tarˌmɛr̥.cɪ/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ɛr̥cɪ|s=5}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|grammar}} an [[infinitive]] [[particle]], an [[infinitive marker]], an indeclinable [[particle]] in front of a [[verb]] in the [[infinitive]]
#: {{uxi|is|að [[tala]]|t=to [[speak]]}}
#: {{uxi|is|að [[lesa]]|t=to [[read]]}}
#: {{uxi|is|að [[fara]]|t=to [[leave]]}}
#: {{uxi|is|að [[hoppa]]|t=to [[jump]]}}

====Usage notes====
* The word {{m|is|að||to}} is the only '''nafnháttarmerki''' in all of Icelandic.
* The '''nafnháttarmerki''' is not used after the verbs {{m|is|munu}}, {{m|is|skulu}}, {{m|is|mega}} and {{m|is|vilja}}.
*: {{uxi|is|Ég skal [[koma]].|t=I shall [[come]].}}
* When enumerating, the '''nafnháttarmerki''' doesn't appear the latter or later adjacent enumerations.
*: {{uxi|is|Hann kann hvorki '''að''' lesa né skrifa.|t=He can neither read nor write}}
*: {{uxi|is|Ég kann '''að''' hoppa, ganga og hlaupa.|t=I know how '''to''' jump, walk and run.}}

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|n}}

===References===
* {{R:Islex}}
