Page 11235 nifl: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
In compounds probably means “darkness”,<ref name="etym">[[w:is:Ásgeir Blöndal Magnússon|Ásgeir Blöndal Magnússon]]. Page '''667''' of the {{m|is|w:is:Íslensk orðsifjabók|Íslensk orðsifjabók|Book of Icelandic Etymology}}. Publisher: {{m|is|w:is:Stofnun Árna Magnússonar á Íslandi|Stofnun Árna Magnússonar á Íslandi|[[w:Árni Magnússon Institute for Icelandic Studies|Árni Magnússon Institute for Icelandic Studies]]}}, first print November 1989 {{ISBN|978-9979-654-01-8}}</ref> ultimately from {{der|is|ine-pro|*nébʰos||cloud}} whence the {{der|is|gem-pro|*nebulaz}}, cognates with Old High German {{m|goh|nebul||fog}}<ref name="etym" /> (New High German {{m|de|nebel}},<ref name="etym" /> whence {{m|de|Nebel||fog, mist, haze; nebula}}) and Latin {{m|la|nebula||fog; cloud; vapor}}.<ref name="etym" />

Compare {{m|is|njóla||night}} {{q|poetic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/nɪpl/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ɪpl|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|poetic}} [[fog]], [[darkness]]<ref name="etym" />

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|n.sg}}

====Derived terms====
