Page 11639 -ó: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Likely influenced by ending of loanwords such as e.g. {{m|is|limbó}}, {{m|is|lottó}}, {{m|is|lúdó}}, {{m|is|póló}} (all names of games), as well as shortened words such as {{m|is|bíó}} (from Danish {{m|da|bio}}, a clipping of {{m|da|biograf}}), which already had {{m|is||-ó-}} ({{m|da||-o-}}) in them before being shortened. Perhaps derived from {{der|is|en|-o#Etymology_1|-o}}. {{etystub|is|Needs more on different semantic categories and parts of speech, e.g. proper names and adjectives; a timeline of developments would also be nice}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ouː/}}

===Suffix===
{{head|is|suffix|g=n}}

# {{lb|is|informal}} {{ng|a suffix used to create colloquial shortenings, usually consisting of the first syllable of the word + {{m|is||-ó}} (these can be nouns, adjectives, and, more rarely, adverbs)}}

