Page 11642 ó-: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|ó-}}, {{m|non|ú-}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*un-}}, from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*n̥-}}, a prefix use of the particle {{m|ine-pro|*ne||not}}. In Icelandic this changed very early from {{m|is|ú-}} to {{m|is|ó-}}.

Cognate with {{cog|ang|un-}} ({{cog|en|un-}}), {{cog|osx|un-}}, {{cog|nl|on-}}, {{cog|goh|un-}} ({{cog|de|un-}}), {{cog|sv|o-}}, {{cog|no|u}}{{,}} and {{cog|got|𐌿𐌽-}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|grc|ἀ-}}, {{m|grc|ἀν-}}, {{cog|la|in-}}{{,}} and {{cog|sga|in-}}.

===Prefix===
{{head|is|prefix}}

# [[un-]], [[non-]], [[in-]]
#: {{prefixusex|is|friður|gloss1=peace|ófriður|gloss2=war}}
#: {{prefixusex|is|heppni|gloss1=luck|óheppni|gloss2=bad luck}}
#: {{prefixusex|is|þekkur|gloss1=well-behaved|óþekkur|gloss2=naughty}}
#: {{prefixusex|is|happ|gloss1=a stroke of luck|óhapp|gloss2=accident}}
#: {{prefixusex|is|samlína|gloss1=collinear|ósamlína|gloss2=noncollinear}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|is}}
* {{l|is|óendanlegur||endless, infinite}}
* {{l|is|óbundinn}}
* {{l|is|óheppni}}
* {{l|is|óhittni}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|ú-}}

-------- end text --------
