{{bor+|is|da|orange}}, from {{der|is|fr|orange||orange (fruit, color)}}, from {{der|is|fro|pome orenge|t=Persian orange}}, literally “orange apple”, influenced by {{der|is|pro|auranja}} and calqued from {{der|is|roa-oit|melarancio}}, {{m|it|melarancia}}, compound of {{m|it|mela|t=apple}} and {{m|it|arancia|(n)arancia|t=orange}}, from {{der|is|ar|نَارَنْج}}, from {{der|is|fa|نارنگ|tr=nârang}}, from {{der|is|sa|नारङ्ग|t=orange tree}}, from {{der|is|dra}} (compare {{cog|ta|நார்த்தங்காய்}}, compound of {{m|ta|நரந்தம்|t=fragrance}} and {{m|ta|காய்|t=fruit}}; also {{cog|te|నారంగము}}, {{cog|ml|നാരങ്ങ}}, {{cog|kn|ಕಿತ್ತಳೆ}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈouːrans/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ouːrans|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{head|is|adjective|invariable}}

# {{lb|is|dated}} [[orange]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|orange}} {{l|is|appelsínugulur}}

===See also===
{{table:colors/is}}

{{C|is|Colors}}
