Composed of {{com|is|púður|t1=powder|sykur|t2=sugar}}.
{{calque|is|da|puddersukker}} (which today refers to brown sugar, but originally referred to finely ground (therefore, presumably, called “powdered”) raw sugar), itself from {{cog|de|Puderzucker}}.

False friend of {{cog|en|powdered sugar}} and {{cog|de|Puderzucker}}, which are instead called {{m|is|flórsykur}} in Icelandic.

