# [[red fescue]] ({{taxlink|Festuca rubra|species}})
#* {{quote-journal|is|year=1926|journal=Ársrit Rætunarfélags Norðurlands|volume=23|page=61|url=http://timarit.is/view_page_init.jsp?issId=229282&pageId=3113436&lang=is&q=rau%F0vingull|title=Sáðsljettur|passage=''Fræið spíraði illa og frægresið hvarf úr sögunni á fáum árum, en í þess stað náði margskonar illgresi yfirhöndinni, svo sem: súrur, mjaðurt, sóleyjar, fíflar o. fl. og grastegundir, sem í Danmörku þykja ljelegar fóðurjurtir, eins og snarrótarpuntur og '''rauðvingull'''.''|translation=The seed sprouted badly and the seed grass disappeared from history in a few years, but in its place many different kinds of weeds gained the upper hand: sorrels, meadowsweet, buttercups, dandelions and others; and grass species, which in Denmark are considered poor fodder plants, like tufted hairgrass and '''red fescue'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|is|date=13 January 1995|journal=Dagblaðið Vísir|title=Ýmsar grastegundir|volume=85/21|issue=11|page=37|url=http://timarit.is/view_page_init.jsp?issId=195849&pageId=2723499&lang=is&q=rau%F0vingull|passage=''Á Íslandi er túnvingull algengasta grastegundin, ef með er talinn '''rauðvingull''', sem stundum telst til sömu tegundar.''|translation=In Iceland, Arctic fescue is the most common grass species, if '''red fescue''' is also counted, which is sometimes considered to be the same species.}}

