From {{der|is|non|-}} ''[[#Etymology 1 4|renna]]'' (1), from earlier {{m|non|rinna}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*rinnaną}}; the alteration i > e is due to influence from the weak verb ''[[#Etymology 2 4|renna]]'' (2) (whence Icelandic [[#Etymology 3 2|renna]] (3)).

====Verb====
{{is-verb-strong|rann|runnu|runnið}}

# {{lb|is|of liquid}} to [[flow]], [[run]]
#: {{ux|is|[[Saxelfur]] '''rennur''' um [[Tékkland]] og [[Þýskaland]].|The [[Elbe]] flows through the [[Czech Republic]] and [[Germany]].|inline=1}}
# {{lb|is|of anything solid}} to [[glide]], [[slide]] {{gloss|move over a surface}}
#: {{ux|is|[[skeið|Skeiðin]] '''rann''' eftir [[endilangur|endilöngu]] [[eldhúsborð]]inu.|The spoon slid the whole length of the kitchen table.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|is|of a person}} to [[slip]], [[slide]] {{gloss|lose one’s balance on a slippery surface}}
#: {{ux|is|[[Kormákur]] '''rann''' á ísnum og [[lenda|lenti]] á [[höfuð|höfðinu]].|Cormac slipped on the ice and fell on his head.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|is|archaic}} to [[run]] (''move quickly'')
# to [[rise]], [[grow]]
# to [[melt]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{is-conj-s3|r|e|nn|mp=-}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|flow}} {{l|is|flæða}}, {{l|is|leka}}
* {{sense|slip, lose one’s balance}} {{l|is|skrika}}
* {{sense|run, i.e. move quickly}} {{l|is|hlaupa}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|is|non|-}} ''[[#Etymology 2 4|renna]]'' (2), from {{der|is|gem-pro|*rannijaną}}. Causative of ''[[#Etymology 2 2|renna]]'' (2).

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|renndi|rennt}}

# to cause (a liquid) to [[flow]]; to [[pour]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
# to [[melt]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
# to cause (e.g. a horse) to run {{+obj|is|dat}}
# to [[slide]] (something or someone) (across a surface or downhill) {{+obj|is|dat}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{is-conj-w2|r|e|nn|mp=-}}

[[Category:Most used Icelandic verbs]]

