===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|róa}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*rōaną}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*h₁reh₁-}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-ri|reri|11=réri|róið}}

# to [[row]], to propel a vessel with [[oar]]s
# to [[sail]] out to [[fish]]
# to [[rock]] [[backwards]] and [[forwards]]

=====Usage notes=====
* One of the four [[w:is:Ri-sagnir|ri-verbs]] in Icelandic, the other being {{m|is|núa||to rub, massage; to wipe}}, {{m|is|snúa||to turn}} and {{m|is|gróa||to grow; to heal}}.
* As with the other ri-verbs, the past tense {{m|is||reri}} was originally pronounced with an ''e'' sound but is today pronounced with a ''[[é]]'' sound. There are therefore two spelling variants used: {{m|is||reri}} and {{m|is||réri}}. The Icelandic Ministry of Education considers both variants to be equally correct,<ref>[https://ritreglur.arnastofnun.is/ Icelandic Ministry of Education - Announcements regarding orthography from 2016 and 2018, section 3.5.5]</ref> but many speakers consider the original {{m|is||reri}} spelling to be the more correct one.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|row}} {{l|is|knýja árum}}
* {{sense|sail out to fish}} {{l|is|róa til fiskjar}}
* {{sense|rock backwards and forwards}} {{l|is|rugga}}

