Page 12846 Rúrik: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from English and Scandinavian languages. The popular serial novel ''[[w:The Gunmaker of Moscow|The Gunmaker of Moscow]]'' by American author [[w:Sylvanus Cobb, Jr.|Sylvanus Cobb, Jr.]], available in Icelandic translation as {{m|is||Valdimar munkur}}, seems to have influenced the earliest uses of the name in Iceland. At least one person in Iceland (born 1903) was named {{m|is||Rúrik Nevel}}, after the book’s protagonist ({{m|en||Ruric Nevel}} in the original). The forms in English ({{m|en|Ruric}}, {{m|en|Rurik}}) and Scandinavian (Danish {{m|da|Rurik}}, Swedish {{m|sv|Rurik}}) are borrowed from {{der|is|ru|Рю́рик}}, itself borrowed from an Eastern variant of {{der|is|non|Hrœrekr}}, ultimately from {{der|is|gem-pro|*Hrōþirīks}}, whence also the Icelandic form {{m|is|Hrærekur}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈruːrɪk/}}

===Proper noun===
{{is-proper noun|@@}}

# {{given name|is|male}}
# {{lb|is|historical}} A [[dynasty]] that ruled over [[Russia]] and was succeded by the [[Romanov]] Dynasty.

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|m.dat-}}

===References===
* {{R:islendingabok.is}}
* {{R:is:NÍ|Rúrik}}
