Page 12889 ræðari: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Attested since the 18th century. Same as Faroese {{m|fo|røðari}}. Ásgeir Blöndal Magnússon does not give the exact derivation, but the Icelandic and Faroese forms are probably derived from a late Old Norse form {{m|non||*rœðari}}. Compare the attested Old Norse forms {{m|non|rœði}} and {{m|non|rœðir}} and German {{m|de|Ruderer}}. Ultimately from the root of the verb {{m|is|róa||to row}} (Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*rōaną}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈraiːðarɪ/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|aiːðarɪ|s=3}}

