===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|is|salibuna}}

===Etymology===
Likely from {{bor|is|da|salig||exhilarated}} + Icelandic {{m|is|buna||downhill ride}}.<ref name=visindavefurinn>[https://www.visindavefur.is/svar.php?id=52958 Guðrún Kvaran. „Hvað merkir orðið salíbuna? Er það viðurkennt íslenskt orð?“ Vísindavefurinn, 2009.]</ref>

Appears in print in the mid-1950s.<ref>[https://timarit.is/page/2766535?iabr=on#page/n3/mode/2up/search/sal%C3%ADbuna/inflections/true "Bæjarpósturinn". Þjóðviljinn - 56. tölublað (09.03.1954), p. 4]</ref> Was noted as an informal word limited to children's speech.<ref>[https://timarit.is/page/2249786?iabr=on#page/n0/mode/2up/search/sal%C3%ADbuna/inflections/true Alþýðublaðið - Issue 270 (30.11.1961) p. 1]</ref><ref>[https://sarpur.is/Adfang.aspx?AdfangID=542834 Sarpur. Þjóðhættir. Answer number 4379. Received 1.1.1977]</ref><ref name=visindavefurinn/>

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# a single [[exhilarate|exhilarating]] [[downhill]] ride (on a [[sled]], on [[ski]]s, or down a playground [[slide]])

