From {{inh|is|non|sál}}, from {{der|is|ang|sāwol}}, from {{der|is|gmw-pro|*saiwalu|*saiwlu}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*saiwalu}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*saiwalō}}.<ref>{{R:is:Íslensk orðsifjabók|1 sál}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:soul}}

# a [[soul]]
#* [[w:Einar Benediktsson|Einar Benediktsson]]
#*: {{quote|is|Aðgát skal höfð í nærveru '''sálar'''.|Exercise caution in the presence of a '''soul'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Blóð er gjaldmiðill '''sálarinnar'''.|Blood is the currency of the '''soul'''.}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|f|id=soul}}

===Etymology 2===
Attested since the 16th century; origin uncertain. Perhaps from {{der|is|gem-pro|*sahalō}}, from the root {{m|gem-pro|*seh-||to cut}}, originally denoting a bag sewn from cut-out pieces of skin; or perhaps from {{m|gem-pro|*sawalō}}, related to {{m|is|sjóður||purse}}, or from {{m|gem-pro|*saihalō}}, related to {{m|is|sár||cask}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:skinbag}}

# a [[skin]] [[bag]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|f,,ar|id=skinbag}}

===References===
<references/>
* {{R:Íslensk orðsifjabók 1989}}

