Page 13245 sei sei: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|is|sei-sei}}
* {{alt|is|sei, sei}}

===Etymology===
Ásgeir Blöndal suggest that this is derived from a {{w|demonstrative}} (e.g. "that thing") related to {{m|is|-si}} (an Old Norse demonstrative adverb or suffix, used for example in {{m|is|þessi|þe'''ssi'''}}) and {{m|is|sá||that thing}}.<ref>{{R:is:Íslensk orðsifjabók|sei}}</ref>
{{m|is||Sei}} does not exist in other contexts in Icelandic.

===Interjection===
{{head|is|intj}}

# {{ng|indicates mild surprise}}; oh [[wow]]; [[oh dear]]
#: {{syn|is|je minn|ja hér|ja hérna|jii|þú segir það|alt5=já, þú segir það}}
#: {{uxi|is|'''Sei sei''', mikil ósköp.|Oh my.}}
# {{ng|indicates mild disapproval}}; [[tsk tsk]]; [[hmph]]
#: {{syn|is|fuss|svei|iss}}
#: {{uxi|is|'''Sei sei''', segja margir íbúar Amsterdam við vaxandi fjölda ferðamanna.|"[[hmph|Hmph]]!" is what many people living in Amsterdam have to say about the increasing number of tourists.|ref=<ref>[https://www.mbl.is/frettir/erlent/2018/01/10/hertar_reglur_um_airbnb_i_amsterdam/ Morgunblaðið, 10 January 2018. Hertar reglur um Airbnb í Amsterdam.]</ref>}}
# {{ng|indicates mild emphasis}}; [[indeed]]
#: {{syn|is|svei mér þá|sannarlega}}
#: {{uxi|is|Hinn bernski undirtónn er vissulega til staðar í öllum myndunum, '''sei sei''' jú.|The child-like undertone is certainly visible in all of his films, oh yes indeed.|ref=<ref>[https://www.mbl.is/greinasafn/grein/397677/ Morgunblaðið, 12 May 1998. Undirvitund og minni.]</ref>}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|sisona}}

