===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|sem||as, like}}, possibly from {{der|is|gem-pro|*samaz||same, alike}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/sɛːm/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ɛːm|s=1}}
* {{qualifier|before words beginning with a consonant}} {{IPA|is|/sɛm/}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|is|conjunction}}

# {{lb|is|with a noun phrase}} [[as]], [[like]]
#: {{ux|is|Hann var '''sem''' guð meðal manna.|t=He was '''like''' a god amongst men.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hár hennar var hvítt '''sem''' snjór.|t=Her hair was white '''as''' snow.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hann er '''sem''' nýr.|t=He is '''as''' [good as] new.}}
#: {{ux|is|[[vista|Vista]] '''sem'''…|t=Save '''as'''…}}
# {{lb|is|with a clause}} [[like]], [[as if]]
#: {{ux|is|Svo virðist '''sem''' sjúkdómurinn sé arfgengur|t=Is seems as though the disease is hereditary.}}
# {{lb|is|relative|with a clause}} [[who]], [[which]], [[that]]
#: {{ux|is|Þetta er maðurinn '''sem''' ég hitti í gær.|t=That’s the man '''that''' I met yesterday.}}
#: {{ux|is|Þetta er konan '''sem''' barði mig.|t=That’s the woman '''who''' hit me.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|as, like, as if}} {{l|is|eins og}}
* {{sense|which, that}} {{l|is|er}}

