#* Genesis 5:3 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20bók%20Móse+5:3&version=ICELAND Icelandic], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20b%C3%B3k%20M%C3%B3se%205:3&version=NIV English])
#*: {{quote|is|Adam lifði hundrað og þrjátíu ár. Þá gat hann son í líking sinni, eftir '''sinni''' mynd, og nefndi hann Set.|When Adam had lived 130 years, he had a son in his own likeness, in '''his own''' image; and he named him Seth.}}
#* '''1928''', [[w:is:Krummavísa|Krummavísa]] (“Raven Song”, on the [[w:source:Krummavísa|Icelandic Wikisource]]) by [[w:is:Jón Ásgeirsson|Jón Ásgeirsson]]
#*: {{quote|is|Krummi krunkar úti,<br/>kallar á nafna '''sinn''':<br/>„Ég fann höfuð af hrúti<br/>hrygg og gæruskinn.“<br/>Komdu nú og kroppaðu með mér,<br/>krummi nafni minn.|Krummi croaks outside,<br/>calling '''his''' namesake:<br/>“I found the head of a ram,<br/>backbone and sheepskin.”<br/>Come now and peck with me,<br/>Krummi, my namesake.”}}

