Page 13496 sinn er siður í landi hverju: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|its [own] is the custom in each land|each country has its own customs}}.

Compare {{cog|fo|sær er siður á landi}}.

===Phrase===
{{head|is|phrase|head=[[sinn]] [[vera|er]] [[siður]] [[í]] [[land|landi]] [[hver|hverju]]}}

# [[when in Rome, do as the Romans do]]

{{cln|is|proverbs}}
-------- end text --------
Page 13497 sinn hver: -------- begin text --------

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun}}

# {{ng|for each [subject] to have its own [object] separately, used when the number of [subjects] is 3 or more}}
#: {{uxi|is|Við þrjú þessi elstu vorum fædd '''sitt''' á '''hverju árinu'''.|The three oldest of us were each born on a separate (consecutive) year.}}

====Usage notes====
{{m|is|sinn|Sinn}} inflects with the subject, {{m|is|hver}} with the object.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|sitt hvað||various things}}
* {{l|is|sitt lítið af hverju||a bit from each category}}
* {{l|is|sitt sýnist hverjum||opinion is divided}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|sinn hvor}} {{q|pronoun used for two items}}
* {{l|is|sitt á hvað||alternating between}}

{{cln|is|indefinite pronouns}}
-------- end text --------
Page 13498 sinn hvor: -------- begin text --------

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun}}

# {{ng|for each [subject] to have its own [object] separately, used when there are two [subjects]}}
#: {{coi|is|að gera eitthvað '''sitt''' í '''hvoru''' lagi|to do something separately}}
#: {{uxi|is|Þeir fóru '''sinn''' á '''hvorum''' bílnum.|They went on separate cars.}}

====Usage notes====
{{m|is|sinn|Sinn}} is supposed to inflect with the subject, {{m|is|hvor}} with the object.
However, this rule is not followed by modern speakers, who instead treat {{m|is|sitt hvor}} as a single word:
* {{uxi|is|Þeir fóru á '''sitt hvorum''' bílnum.|They went on separate cars.}}
* {{coi|is|að gera eitthvað í '''sitt hvoru''' lagi|to do something separately}}
* {{uxi|is|Viljið þið borga saman eða í '''sitt hvoru''' lagi?|Do you want to pay together or separately?}}
While it is considered incorrect by language authorities, this usage is common in formal situations and in newspapers.

Also relatively common but also [[proscribe]]d is to inflect {{m|is||sinn}} with the object:
* {{uxi|is|Þeir fóru á '''sínum hvorum''' bílnum.|They went on separate cars.}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|sinn hver}} {{q|pronoun used for three or more items}}
* {{l|is|sitt á hvað||alternating between}}
* {{l|is|sitt hvoru megin}}

{{cln|is|indefinite pronouns}}
