Page 13883 skina: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|is|ɪːna|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
Related to {{cog|nn|[[skine|skĭne]]}}, {{cog|sv|skena||small, thin plate}}; {{cog|goh|skina}}, {{cog|dum|scene||metal or wooden plate; shinbone}}; {{cog|ang|scinu}} (whence {{cog|en|shin}}). Compare also {{cog|ang|scīa||shin}}, {{cog|gmh|schīe||fencepost}}. From {{der|is|ine-pro|*skē̆i-||split, cleave, separate}}, whence also {{cog|la|sciō||to know}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:keyholeplate}}

# a small [[plate]] [[cover]]ing a [[keyhole]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|f|id=keyholeplate}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|is|skinna}}
* {{l|is|skráarlauf}}

===Etymology 2===
Neologism, probably related to {{m|is|skína||to shine}}, {{m|is|skin||shine}} and Etymology 3, probably referring to the peritoneum's thin, transparent quality.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:peritoneum}}

# [[peritoneum]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|f|id=peritoneum}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|is|lífhimna}}
* {{l|is|holhimna}}

===Etymology 3===
Probably related to {{m|is|skína||to shine}}, {{m|is|skin||shine}}, likely in reference to the fish's light color. Compare with the synonym {{m|is|lýsa}}, related to the verb {{m|is|lýsa||to emit light}}, the noun {{m|is|ljós||light}} and adjective {{m|is|ljós||light}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:whiting}}

# {{lb|is|dialectal}} [[whiting]] ({{taxfmt|Merlangius merlangus|species}})

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|f|id=whiting}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|is|lýsa}}
* {{l|is|jakobsfiskur}}
* {{l|is|lundaseiði}}

===Etymology 4===
Cf. {{cog|nn|[[skina|skĭna]]}}, {{cog|nn|skjena||to run off because of mosquitoes {{q|of cows}}}}, {{cog|sv|skena}} and {{cog|jut|skjenne||to shy {{q|of a horse}}}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|skinaði|skinað}}

# to go [[crazy]], be driven [[mad]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{rfinfl|is|verb}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|is|brjálast}}
* {{l|is|ganga af göflunum}}
* {{l|is|geggjast}}
* {{l|is|sturlast}}
* {{l|is|ærast}}

===Etymology 5===
Probably related to {{m|is|skína||to shine}}, {{m|is|skin||shine}} and Etymology 3, referring to the light, transparent look of diarrheic feces.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:diarrhea}}

# [[thin]] and rather [[liquid]] [[excrement]]; [[diarrheic]] [[feces]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|f|id=diarrhea}}

