Page 14540 sokkaleistur: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|is|sokkaleisti}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# a low cut [[sock]]
#* {{cite-web|titleurl=https://www.bbl.is/media/1/bbl-20.-tbl.-2015-web.pdf|text='''Sokkaleistarnir''' eru heklaðir úr grófgerðu garni|work=Bændablaðið|page=73|date=22 October 2015|title=Heklaðir '''sokkaleistar'''}}
# the sole of a sock
#: {{uxi|is|'''Sokkaleistarnir''' mínir voru orðnir gegnblautir.|The soles of my socks had become wet.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Kulda frá gólfinu lagði í gegnum '''sokkaleistana'''.|The cold temperature of the floor made its way through the soles of my socks.}}
# {{lb|is|in the phrase "'''á sokkaleistunum'''"}} to be [[shoeless]] {{gloss|to be wearing socks but not shoes, often in a situation where shoes would be expected such as outside}}
#: {{uxi|is|Hann hljóp út '''á sokkaleistunum'''.|He ran out of the house without putting shoes on.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Þingmaðurinn var '''á sokkaleistunum''' í þingsal.|The member of parliament wasn't wearing shoes in the parliament hall.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Ég er 175 cm á hæð '''á sokkaleistunum'''.|I am 175 cm tall (measured while wearing my socks).}}

====Usage notes====
Only the last meaning ("á sokkaleistunum") is common in modern Icelandic, the first two meanings are sufficiently rare that many speakers are not familiar with them.

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|m}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|berfættur||barefoot}}
