Page 15288 sulla: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|sulla|t=to swill}}, perhaps from {{der|is|non|sollr}}, {{m|non|*sullr|t=swill, slop for pigs}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*swulaz|t=swill}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*swel-|t=to wash, wash down, gulp, swallow}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|swill}}. Compare also {{cog|non|svalla|t=to drink heavily, swill}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈsʏtla/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ʏtla|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|sullaði|sullað}}

# to [[splash]] around, to splash about
#: ''Ég vil '''sulla''' í [[pollur|pollinum]]!''
#:: I wanna go '''splashing about''' in the [[puddle]]!
#: {{ux|is|Þetta er mynd af Önnu að '''sulla'''.|This is a picture of Anna '''splashing'''.}}
# to [[spill]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''sullaði''' mjólkinni.|I '''spilled''' the milk.}}

====Usage notes====
* The verb {{m|is|sulla}} and {{m|is|sulla saman||to mix together}} denote a hint of apathy, carelessness or casualness of the doer's actions.
* This verb may be found childish.
* In the sense of "[[spilling]]" the preposition {{m|is|á||on}} may be added to give information as to where one spilled something:
*: ''Ég '''sullaði''' mjólk á gólfið.''
*:: I '''spilled''' milk on the floor.

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-w4|s|u|ll}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|sulla á||to [[spill]] on}}
* {{l|is|sulla saman||to mix something}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|sull}}

-------- end text --------
