Page 15368 svangur: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|hungur|lang=is}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈsvauŋkʏr/}}
* {{rhymes|is|auŋkʏr|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|svangr||slender, slim, thin}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*swangaz||thin, slim}}. The original meaning in Germanic was probably 'curved inwards', discernible from the derived Old Norse {{m|non|svangi||flank, groin}}, i.e., 'the sides of the abdomen which curve inwards slightly'. Within Icelandic the meaning developed from 'thin' to 'feeling hungry'.<ref>{{R:gem:EWGP|head=swanga-|page=572}}</ref> Cognates are {{cog|fo|svangur||hungry}}, {{cog|da|svang||thin, famished}}, {{cog|no|svang||hungry}}, dialectal {{cog|sv|svånger||thin, hungry, empty}}, Middle {{cog|sv|svanger||slender, emaciated, very thin}}, {{cog|gmh|swanger||flexible, slender}}.<ref name="blondal">{{R:Íslensk orðsifjabók 1989}}</ref><ref>{{R:non:AnEW|head=svangr|page=564}}</ref>

Further origin unsure, perhaps related to Old Irish {{m|sga|seng||narrow, thin}}. Not related to Danish {{m|da|svanger}}, Norwegian {{m|no|svanger}}, Dutch {{m|nl|zwanger}}, and German {{m|de|schwanger||pregnant}}.

====Adjective====
{{is-adj|svengri|comp2=svangari|svengstur|sup2=svangastur}}

# [[hungry]], [[peckish]]
#: {{ux|is|Ertu '''svöng'''?|Are you '''hungry'''?}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég er mjög '''svangur'''.|I'm really '''hungry'''.}}
# {{lb|is|obsolete}} [[thin]], [[slender]], [[slim]]

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|hungry}} {{l|is|hungraður}},<ref name="blondal" /> {{l|is|soltinn}}<ref name="blondal" />
* {{sense|obsolete: thin}} {{l|is|mjór}}, {{l|is|grannur}},<ref name="blondal" /> {{l|is|magur}}, {{l|is|mjósleginn}}<ref name="blondal" />

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|ég er svangur||[[I am hungry]]}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|is|svangi||flank, groin}}
* {{l|is|svengd||hunger}}
* {{l|is|svengja||to be hungry}}

=====See also=====
* [[hungraður]]

===Etymology 2===
A noun of the adjectival form {{m|is|svangur||hungry; thin}}. Compare the {{der|is|non|svangi||the groins, especially of animals}} which was also spelled {{m|non|svangr||the groins, especially of animals}}.

{{wikipedia|lang=is}}
{{wikipedia|magi|lang=is}}

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@}}

# an [[empty]] or [[hungry]] [[stomach]]; used in set phrases
#: {{ux|is|Ég held að ég [[fá sér í svanginn|fái mér eitthvað í '''svanginn''']].|I think I'll get something to eat.}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|m.sg.dat-/-}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In modern Icelandic, this word is predominantly used in the [[accusative case]] with a [[definite article]] ({{m|is||svanginn}}) in the set phrase {{m|is|fá sér í svanginn|fá sér eitthvað í svanginn|to get something to eat}}.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|fá sér í svanginn||to get something to eat}}

