Page 15513 svunta: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|is|svinta}}, which is still preserved in East Iceland. First attested in the 16th century. Cognate with {{cog|fo|svinta}}, {{cog|no|svinte}} (whence the Icelandic word may have come). Probably related to Norwegian {{m|no|svinte||to swing, wave}}, which might be a loan word from an unattested Middle Low German source and ultimately from {{der|is|gem-pro|*swingatją}} and related to Middle High German {{m|gmh|swanzen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈsvʏn̥ta/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ʏn̥ta|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[apron]]
# [[counterfoil]], the part of a [[cheque]] that is retained in the [[chequebook]] as a record; a [[stub]]

