Page 15616 sæll: -------- begin text --------
{{phrasebook|is}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|sæll||happy}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*sēliz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/saitl̥/|[sai̯tɬ]}}
* {{rhymes|is|aitl|s=1}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|sælari|sælastur}}

# [[happy]], [[content]]
#: {{syn|is|ánægður|hamingjusamur|líða|alt3=líða vel}}
## [[fortunate]]
## my [[dear]] {{gloss|used in certain set phrases when addressing someone}}
##: {{coi|is|sonur '''sæll'''|my dear '''son'''}}
# [[hello]] {{gloss|a greeting}}

====Usage notes====
{{m|is||Sæll}} is a very common greeting, particularly in formal situations. It inflects with the gender and plurality of the person being addressed ({{m|is||sæll}} for a man, {{m|is||sæl}} for a woman and a mixed-gender group, {{m|is||sælir}} for a group of men, and {{m|is||sælar}} for a group of women).

In slang, the plural {{m|is||sælir}}/{{m|is||sælar}} is occasionally used to address a single person; it is considered a more "cool" and relaxed greeting.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-adj-3|s|æ|l}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|sæll vertu||hello}}
* {{l|is|vertu sæll||goodbye}}
* {{l|is|sæll og blessaður||hello}}
* {{l|is|sæla||happiness}}

===References===
* {{R:Íslensk orðsifjabók 1989}}

-------- end text --------
