Page 15713 takk: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|is|da|tak}}, from {{der|is|non|þǫkk}} (whence inherited {{cog|is|þökk}}), from {{der|is|gem-pro|*þankō}}, {{m|gem-pro|*þankaz}}. Cognates include [[w:Faroese language|Faroese]] and [[w:Norwegian language|Norwegian]] ''takk'', {{cog|da|tak}}, {{cog|sv|tack}}, {{cog|en|thank}}, {{cog|fy|tank}}, {{cog|nl|dank}} and {{cog|de|Dank}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|is|/ˈtʰahk/}}

===Interjection===
{{head|is|interjection}}

# [[thank you]], [[thanks]]
# [[please]]: {{non-gloss|used to make a polite request}}.
#: {{ux
|is|Einn kaffibolla, '''takk'''.|One cup of coffee, please.
}}
#: {{ux
|is|Já, '''takk'''.|Yes, please.
}}

====Usage notes====
* The interjection '''takk''' (borrowed from [[w:Danish|Danish]]) is a cognate of ''{{l|is|þökk||a thank, thanks}}'', itself inherited directly from Old Norse.
* The term ''þökk'' is used as a noun, and rarely as an interjection by itself. The derived term ''{{l|is|þökk fyrir}}'' can be used as an interjection.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|is|takk fyrir}}
* {{l|is|þökk}}
* {{l|is|þökk fyrir}}
* {{l|is|þakka þér}} {{q|singular}}; {{l|is|þakka yður}} {{q|singular, formal; rare}}
* {{l|is|þakka þér fyrir}} {{q|singular}}; {{l|is|þakka yður fyrir}} {{q|singular, formal; rare}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í dag||thanks for today}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í gær||thanks for yesterday}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í kvöld||thanks for tonight}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir mig||thanks for myself}} {{q|commonly said to a host for having been received as a guest; both after dining and when departing}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir síðast}}, {{l|is|takk fyrir seinast||thanks for last time}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|þakka||to thank}}
* {{l|is|takk kærlega||thank you ''dearly''; thank you very much}}
* {{l|is|kærar þakkir||''dear'' thanks; thank you very much}}
* {{l|is|þúsund þakkir||thousand thanks}}

-------- end text --------
Page 15714 takk fyrir: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{compound|is|takk|fyrir|t1=thanks|t2=for}}, literally meaning “thanks ''for'' ...”. Cognate with {{cog|is|þökk fyrir}} and {{cog|fo|takk fyri}}, ''{{l|fo|tøkk fyri}}''.

===Interjection===
{{head|is|interjection}}

# [[thank you]], [[thanks]] {{+obj|is|acc}}

====Usage notes====
* The interjection ''{{l|is|takk||thanks}}'' (borrowed from [[w:Danish|Danish]] ''{{l|da|tak}}'', from {{der|is|non|þǫkk}}) is a cognate of ''{{l|is|þökk||a thank, thanks}}'', itself inherited directly from Old Norse.
* The term ''þökk'' is used as a noun, and rarely as an interjection by itself. The derived term ''{{l|is|þökk fyrir}}'' can be used as an interjection.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|is|takk}}
* {{l|is|þökk fyrir}}
* {{l|is|þakka þér}} {{q|singular}} (literally “(I) thank you”)
** {{l|is|þakka þér fyrir}} {{q|singular}} (literally “thank you ''for'' ...”)
** {{l|is|þakka ykkur fyrir}} {{q|plural}} (literally “thank you ''for'' ...”)
* {{l|is|þakka yður}} {{q|singular, formal; rare}} (literally “(I) thank you ...”)
** {{l|is|þakka yður fyrir}} {{q|singular and plural, formal; rare}} (literally “thank you ''for'' ...”)

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í dag||thanks for today}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í gær||thanks for yesterday}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í kvöld||thanks for tonight}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir mig||thanks for myself}} {{q|commonly said to a host for having been received as a guest; both after dining and when departing}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir síðast}}, {{l|is|takk fyrir seinast||thanks for last time}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|þakka||to thank}}
* {{l|is|takk kærlega||thank you ''dearly''; thank you very much}}
* {{l|is|kærar þakkir||''dear'' thanks; thank you very much}}
* {{l|is|þúsund þakkir||thousand thanks}}

