# thank you for the meal (''said after finishing a meal'')

====Usage notes====
This phrase (or the related {{m|is|takk fyrir mig}}) is used after finishing a meal to show gratitude to the person who cooked it or provided it. Forgetting to show gratitude after a meal is considered rude; in many households it is [[obligatory]] for children to say "takk fyrir matinn" after a meal.

''Takk fyrir matinn'' is more informal and is used at home while {{m|is|takk fyrir mig}} is more [[deferential]] and would be used after being invited to dinner.

====See also====
* {{l|is|takk fyrir mig}}
* {{l|is|þakka fyrir sig|að þakka fyrir sig}}
* {{l|is|verði þér að góðu||you're welcome}}
-------- end text --------
Page 15719 takk fyrir mig: -------- begin text --------

===Phrase===
{{head|is|phrase|head=[[takk]] [[fyrir]] [[ég|mig]]}}

# {{ng|said to show gratitude after a meal or an event that one is invited to}}

====Usage notes====
This phrase is used to show gratitude: after finishing a meal you were invited to, when leaving a party you were invited to, after a trip someone took you on, or after a performance (to thank the audience for coming).
It is fairly [[deferential]] and can be used in formal situations.

====See also====
* {{l|is|þakka fyrir sig|að þakka fyrir sig|to show gratitude}}
* {{l|is|verði þér að góðu||you're welcome}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir matinn||thank you for the meal}}
-------- end text --------
