Page 15997 timburmaður: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|is|timbur|t1=timber|maður|t2=man}}. The sense ‘hangover’ is a {{semantic loan|is|da|tømmermænd||a hangover}}. The oldest attestation of ''timburmenn'' in the sense "hangover" in the ''Orðabók Háskólans'' is from an issue of ''Fjallkonan'' from 1891<ref name="visinda">{{webofscience|5992|Hvaðan kemur orðið timburmenn?|Where does the word ''timburmenn'' come from?}}</ref> which goes as follows:

: {{quote|is|Margar tegundir kaffibrauðs ... fínasta Scotch Whisky, hið eina í bænum sem enginn fær af hina leiðu '''timbrmenn'''. |Many types of bakery products ... the finest Scotch Whiskey, the only one in town that does not result in the dreaded '''hangover'''.}}

The literal meaning of ‘carpenter’, however, is far older.<ref name="visinda"/>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈtʰɪmpʏrˌmaːðʏr/}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|used in the plural}} a [[hangover]]{{attention|is|If this sense is only ever used in the plural (as in Danish), it should be moved thither.}}
#: {{syn|is|þynnka}}
# {{lb|is|dated}} [[carpenter]], [[woodworker]]
#: {{syn|is|smiður|trésmiður|húsasmiður|snikkari}}

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|@m}}

