Page 16699 -ur: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|-r}}, the nominative singular ending for ''i-'', ''u-'', masculine ''a-'', and masculine consonant stem nouns, as well as most  masculine adjectives. In turn, the Old Norse endings all stem from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*-s}}, a general-purpose masculine/feminine singular nominative ending.

====Suffix====
{{head|is|suffix|cat2=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{ng|nominative singular ending of most strong masculine nouns}}
# {{ng|nominative singular ending of a few strong masculine nouns}}
# {{ng|nominative singular ending of the majority of strong masculine adjectives}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|is|non|-ur|pos=weak feminine nominative and accusative plural ending}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|is|suffix|cat2=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{ng|the nominative and accusative plural ending for most weak feminine nouns; triggers u-mutation of a preceding ''a''}}

