===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|vald}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*waldą}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/valt/}}
* {{rhymes|is|alt|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|also|_|in the plural}} [[power]], [[authority]]
# [[authority]], [[power]]
#* Timothy 2:11-12 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Timothy+2:11-12&version=NIV English], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1%20Timothy%202:11-12&version=ICELAND Icelandic])
#*: {{quote|is|Konan á að læra í kyrrþey, í allri undirgefni. Ekki leyfi ég konu að kenna eða taka sér '''vald''' yfir manninum, heldur á hún að vera kyrrlát.|A woman should learn in quietness and full submission. I do not permit a woman to teach or to have '''authority''' over a man; she must be silent.}}
#* Revelation 6-11 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/resources/readingplans/index.php/2010/12/29?plan=2&version=31 English] and [http://www.biblegateway.com/resources/readingplans/index.php/2010/12/29?plan=2&version=18 Icelandic])
#*: {{quote|is|Og ég sá, og sjá: Bleikur hestur, og sá er á honum sat, hann hét Dauði, og Hel var í för með honum. Þeim var gefið '''vald''' yfir fjórða hluta jarðarinnar, til þess að deyða með sverði, með hungri og drepsótt og láta menn farast fyrir villidýrum jarðarinnar.|I looked, and there before me was a pale horse! Its rider was named Death, and Hades was following close behind him. They were given '''power''' over a fourth of the earth to kill by sword, famine and plague, and by the wild beasts of the earth.}}
# [[force]], [[violence]]
#: {{ux|is|Með '''valdi'''.|With '''force'''.}}
# {{lb|is|in the plural}} a [[cause]]
#: {{ux|is|Hún dó af þínum '''völdum'''.|She died '''because''' of you.}}

