Page 16991 varið: -------- begin text --------

===Adjective===
{{is-adj}}

# {{q|with "{{l|is|í}}"}} to have good qualities; to have [[merit]]s; to be special and interesting
#: {{syn|is|þykja mikið til einhvers koma}}
#: {{uxi|is|Það er ekkert '''varið í''' þetta.|This thing has no interesting qualities and I would not recommend it.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Er eitthvað '''varið í''' þetta?|Does this thing have any interesting qualities such that you would recommend it to me?}}
# {{q|with "{{l|is|þannig}}" or "{{l|is|svo}}"}} for things to be that way
#: {{uxi|is|En því er ekki svo '''varið'''.|But that is not the case.}}

====Usage notes====
This adjective only exists in the neuter and only in certain set phrases.

The first meaning is most often used with negation ("ekkert varið í þetta") or in questions that imply the assumption of a negative answer ("Er eitthvað varið í þetta?"), although it can be used positively ("Það er mikið í hann varið").

===Verb===
{{head|is|verb form}}

# {{inflection of|is|vara||2|pl|pres|ind//subj|act}}
# {{inflection of|is|vara||2|pl|imp|act}}
# {{inflection of|is|verja||supine}}
#: {{uxi|is|Ég hef '''varið''' miklum tíma í þetta.|I've spent a lot of time on this.}}

===See also===
* {{l|is|varinn}}
-------- end text --------
