#: {{syn|is|karl|karlmaður|maður}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|m.dat-:i/-|id=man}}

===Etymology 2===
A 19th century alteration of earlier {{m|is|vör}}, from {{der|is|non|vǫrr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*warzuz}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|is|var|vör}}

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:oar line}}

# a [[line]] in the [[water]] made by the movement of an [[oar]] or a [[boat]]
#: {{syn|is|árarfar<q:of an oar>|kjölrák<q:of a boat>}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|m,,ir|n.q:or (regionally)|id=oar line}}

===Etymology 3===
{{inh+|is|non|ver}}, of the same meaning. Origin uncertain, but probably related to {{m|is|vari||liquid}} and to {{cog|ang|wær||sea}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:sea}}

# {{lb|is|poetic}} the [[sea]], the [[ocean]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|n.sg|id=sea}}

===Etymology 4===
The same as {{cog|no|vær||fishing harbor, fishing village}}, other cognates including {{cog|ang|wer}} (whence modern {{cog|en|weir}}), {{cog|osx|werr}}, {{cog|gml|were}}/{{m|gml|wer}}, {{cog|gmh|wer}} (whence {{cog|de|Wehr}}). Probably from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*warjaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*warją||dam, weir}}, related to {{m|is|vör|g=f||landing space for a boat}} and to {{m|is|verja||protect}}. The root meaning would then be a guarded or fenced off place.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:facility}}

# [[fishing]] center
# a place where a flock of birds makes its nests {{q|and eggs may be gathered or birds caught}}
# a wet grassy spot in an otherwise inhospitable area; [[oasis]]
#: {{q|in this sense common as a suffix in place names:}} {{m|is|Eyvindarver}}, {{m|is|Þjórsárver}}
# {{lb|is|as a suffix}} production facility
#: {{suffixusex|is|kvikmynd|t1=movie|kvikmyndaver|t2=movie studio, movie production facility}}
#: {{suffixusex|is|ál|t1=aluminum|álver|t2=aluminum production facility}}
# {{n-g|a generic suffix for proper names of community centers, shopping centers, or names of [[businesses]]}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-ndecl|n|id=facility}}

