Page 17306 vér: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|vér}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*wīz}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*wéy}}, plural of {{m|ine-pro|*éǵh₂}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/vjɛːr̥/}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun}}

# {{lb|is|archaic|formal}} First person plural pronoun; [[we]] (singular ''[[ég#Icelandic|ég]]'', ''[[eg#Icelandic|eg]]'').
# {{lb|is|archaic|formal}} A formal term of self-reference used by a royal person; [[we]].
#: '''''Vér''' teljum þetta [[mál]] hið [[alvarlegur|alvarlegasta]]. [[kalla saman|Kallið saman]] [[ríkisráð|ríkisráðið]] [[undir eins]].''
#:: '''We''' deem this matter most grave. Assemble the [[privy council]] immediately.

====Usage notes====
This pronoun has mostly fallen out of use in favour of {{m|is|við}}, but lingers in biblical language in the raw plural sense, and finds occasional use elsewhere. As a majestic self-reference, it was used in royal decrees, and may find modern use e.g. in literature dealing with persons who refer to themselves in such a way.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-formal-ppron-table}}

{{cln|is|personal pronouns}}

