===Etymology===
Modeled after {{m|is|sjúkrabíll||ambulance}}, composed of {{com|is|væla|t1=whine|bíll|t2=car}}. First seen on print in 2008,<ref>[https://timarit.is/page/3624428?iabr=on#page/n37/search/%22v%C3%A6lub%C3%ADlinn%22 24 stundir - 30. janúar 2008]</ref> later popularized by a 2010 children's song.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|sarcastic|derisive}} a hypothetical “ambulance” that comes to the aid of someone whining or complaining
#: {{uxi|is|Á ég að hringja á '''vælubílinn'''?|Stop crying about it, you're being a baby.|lit=Do you want me to call the whining ambulance?}}

====Usage notes====
This phrase is used sarcastically when someone is crying or complaining about something.

