Page 17694 völ: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|vǫl}} (neuter plural or feminine singular). The word might be an Old Norse (or later Icelandic) alteration of an original neuter plural (the plural of {{m|is|val}}), since it is in Old Norse definitely attested in neuter plural but perhaps also in feminine singular, or else the feminine word is inherited from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*walō}} and identical to {{cog|goh|wala||choice}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/vœːl/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|œːl|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[choice]]

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|f,--.sg}}
Note: the genitive is unattested.

