* {{IPA|is|/ˈiːmɪs/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|iːmɪs}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun|feminine|ýmis|neuter|ýmist}}

# [[various]]

====Declension====
{{is-decl-adj-strong||ý|m|i|s}}
The masculine nominative singular ''ýmiss'' also occurs. Also sometimes seen are feminine dative and genitive singular ''ýmissri'', ''ýmissrar'', respectively, and genitive plural ''ýmissra''.

There is also a variant {{m|is|ýms}}, where the ''-i-'' is dropped throughout and the resulting declension is the same as of e.g. {{m|is|frjáls}}:
{{is-decl-adj-strong||ý|ms|title=strong declension (variant)}}

Occasionally this word is also used in the weak declension, usually with an article before it, and sometimes even in superlative. This is, however, proscribed by many authorities.
{{is-decl-adj-weak||ý|ms}}
{{is-decl-adj-weak||ý|ms|a|st|title=superlative (weak declension)}}

