Page 17886 þegar stórt er spurt: -------- begin text --------

===Proverb===
{{head|is|proverb|head=[[þegar]] [[stór]]t er [[spyrja|spurt]]}}

# {{lb|is|idiom}} ''[[ellipsis]] of '''{{l|is|þegar stórt er spurt er oft fátt um svör}}'''''

====Usage notes====
This shortened form is more common than the entire saying.
-------- end text --------
Page 17887 þegar stórt er spurt er oft fátt um svör: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|is|þegar stórt er spurt||[[ellipsis]] of the full saying}}
* þegar stórt er spurt þá er lítið um svör
* þegar stórt er spurt verður oft fátt um svör

===Proverb===
{{head|is|proverb|head=[[þegar]] [[stór]]t er [[spyrja|spurt]] er [[oft]] [[fátt]] [[um]] [[svar|svör]]}}

# {{lb|is|idiom}} {{ng|used to [[graceful]]ly [[dodge]] a question}}; I am unable to give an answer to that question; There are no answers to such big questions

====Usage notes====
The saying literally translates to "to big questions there are few answers / few willing to answer". It sounds wise and proverbial, and for that reason it renders the original [[inquirer]] incapable of continuing his line of questioning. It can be used when one doesn't know the answer or when one doesn't want to answer.

It is more common to shorten this saying to just {{m|is|þegar stórt er spurt}}.
-------- end text --------
