{{is-verb-strong|þaut|þutu|þotið}}

# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[rush]], to [[dash]]
#* ''Á Sprengisandi'' (“On Sprengisandur”) by [[w:en:Grímur Thomsen|Grímur Thomsen]]
#*: Þey þey! þey þey! '''þaut''' í holti tófa,
#*: þurran vill hún blóði væta góm,
#*: eða líka einhver var að hóa
#*: undarlega digrum karlaróm;
#*: útilegumenn í Ódáðahraun
#*: eru kannske að smala fé á laun.
#*:: Hush, hush, hush, hush,
#*:: a vixen '''dashed''' in the hillock,
#*:: wanting to quench her thirst with blood,
#*:: then, there was also someone calling,
#*:: with a strangely deep man's voice;
#*:: Outlaws, to the {{m|is|Ódáðahraun}} (a vast, desolate lava field in the Icelandic highlands)
#*:: are perhaps secretly driving sheep.
# {{lb|is|intransitive|of the wind}} to [[whistle]], [[sing]]
#: {{ux|is|Vindurinn '''þýtur''' og þrumurnar dynja.|The wind '''whistles''' and the thunders roar.}}

