Page 18085 þórðargleði: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{com|is|Þórður|t1=Þórður, an Icelandic male given name|gleði|t2=joy, happiness|lit=joy of Þórður}}. It was coined by reverend Árni Þórarinsson (1860–1948) to describe an event in which Þórður, one of his [[parishioner]]s, laughed at the poor fortune of the people living in the North of Iceland who had suffered [[hay]] rot due to excessive raining that summer.

Although the word {{m|is|Þórður}} is a proper name and is capitalized the compound word {{m|is|þórðargleði}} is not.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20151004181343/http://www.arnastofnun.is/solofile/1011132 II. STÓR OG LÍTILL STAFUR] on [[w:Árnastofnun|Árnastofnun.is]]</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈθourðarklɛːðɪ/}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[schadenfreude]] {{gloss|malicious enjoyment of another person's suffering}}
#: {{syn|is|meinfýsi|hlakka yfir}}

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|f.sg}}

===References===
<references/>

