Page 18099 þórsdagur: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|þórsdagr||Thor's day, day of Thor}} {{m|non|Þórr||Thor}} (modern Icelandic {{m|is|Þór}}) and {{m|is|dagr||a day}} (modern Icelandic {{m|is|dagur||a day}}). Corresponds to {{der|is|gmw-pro|*Þunras dag||day of the thunder god}}, calque of {{der|is|la|dies Iovis}}.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|archaic}} [[Thursday]]

====Usage notes====
* This word was replaced during Iceland's shift to Christianity by {{m|is|fimmtudagur}}, which means simply "[[fifth]] day". It is now considered archaic, but may be used jocularly or by some revivalists.

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|@d}}

====Derived terms====
* {{qualifier|rare|archaic}} {{l|is|hvíti þórsdagur}} ([[Ascension Day]], ''synonymous'' {{l|is|uppstigningardagur}})
* {{qualifier|rare|archaic}} {{l|is|skíri þórsdagur}} ([[Maundy Thursday]], ''synonymous'' {{l|is|skírdagur}})

{{C|is|Days of the week}}
-------- end text --------
