Page 18127 þrátt fyrir: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{unc|is}}. Can either be interpreted as the neuter of {{m|is|þrár}} + {{m|is|fyrir}}, {{lit|stubborn for|nocap=1}}, or as the Old Norse past participle of largely synonymous {{m|non|þrá}} and {{m|non|þreyja|t=to long for}} + {{m|is|fyrir}}, {{lit|(having) longed for|nocap=1}}. Either way, contamination of {{m+|non|í þrá|t=despite}} and {{m|non|fyrir|t=despite}} clearly also played a role.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˌθrauhtˈfɪːrɪr/}}
{{rfap|is}}

===Preposition===
{{head|is|preposition}}

# [[despite]], [[in spite of]] {{+obj|is|acc}}
#: {{coi|is|'''þrátt fyrir''' allt|'''in spite of''' everything}}
#: {{coi|is|'''þrátt fyrir''' það|[[nevertheless]]}}
#* {{quote-book|is|year=1985|author=Elín Pálmadóttir|publisher=Almenna bókafélagið|title=Gerður. Ævisaga myndhöggvara|text=Hún vann að höggmyndum sínum á hverju sem gekk og '''þrátt fyrir''' peningaleysi og alls konar erfiðleika.|t=She worked on her sculptures in whatever way she could, '''despite''' lack of money and all kinds of difficulties.}}

{{cln|is|prepositions that govern the accusative}}
