Page 18387 þökk: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|þǫkk}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*þankō}}, {{m|gem-pro|*þankaz}}. Cognates include {{cog|is|takk}}, {{cog|fo|tøkk}}, {{cog|no|takk}}, {{cog|da|tak}}, {{cog|sv|tack}}, {{cog|en|thank}}, {{cog|fy|tank}}, {{cog|nl|dank}} and {{cog|de|Dank}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/θœhk/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|œhk|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# a [[thank]], [[thanks]]; {{non-gloss|an expression of gratitude}}.

====Usage notes====
* The term '''þökk''' is used as a noun, and rarely as an interjection by itself. The derived term ''{{l|is|þökk fyrir}}'' can be used as an interjection.
* The interjection ''{{l|is|takk||thanks}}'' and its derivations are more common. ''Takk'' is borrowed from [[w:Danish|Danish]] ''{{l|da|tak}}'', itself inherited from {{der|is|non|þǫkk}}, and is thus a cognate of '''þökk'''.

====Declension====
{{is-ndecl|f}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|flytja}} þökk (“bring thanks”)
* {{l|is|færa}} þökk (“bring thanks”)
* {{l|is|gjalda}} þökk (“pay thanks”)
* {{l|is|kunna}} þökk (“be thankful”, literally “know thanks”)
* {{l|is|kærar þakkir||''dear'' thanks; thank you very much}}
* {{l|is|óþökk}}
* {{l|is|tjá}} þökk (“express thanks”)
* {{l|is|þúsund þakkir||thousand thanks}}
* {{l|is|þökk fyrir||thank you}}
* {{l|is|þökk sé||thanks to}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|þakka||to thank}}
* {{l|is|takk}}, {{l|is|takk fyrir||thank you}}
-------- end text --------
