===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|ǿði|g=f}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*wōdį̄}}; compare {{cog|fo|øði|g=f}}. Related to {{m|is|óður}}. The shift in gender from feminine to neuter is presumably due to the influence of {{m|non|ǿði|g=n|t=mind, disposition}}, for which see Etymology 3 below.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|@@:frenzy}}

# [[frenzy]], [[rage]], [[madness]]
#: {{syn|is|klikkun|ofsi|skapofsi}}
# {{lb|is|colloquial}} [[great]], [[excellent]], [[wonderful]]
#: {{syn|is|frábær|alt1=frábært|æðislegur|alt2=æðislegt|magnaður|alt3=magnað}}
#: {{uxi|is|Það væri auðvitað algjört '''æði'''.|That would of course be great.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Ég kem í heimsókn á eftir. – '''Æði'''!|I'll come over for a visit later today. – Great!}}

